{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899439187,"sessionID":"ses_1d155f159ffeoBPFus3a3wVk5t","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_2aVleKKehlMR5KvxPNU7f8oU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\n+title: \"Source-aware load-use gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current interlock compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n+  instruction does not really consume that operand. That can insert avoidable\n+  bubbles after loads on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it also\n+  keeps unnecessary compare logic on the stall path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and feed them into the load-use\n+  interlock so the dependency check only fires when the younger instruction\n+  truly reads that source. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged,\n+  but stop stalling on payload-only register fields and trim the control-path\n+  fanout that currently reaches the PC and IF/ID hold logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the usage bits alongside the decoded instruction bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the usage sideband into the interlock path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage information and remove false stalls on instructions that do not read the loaded operand.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bone