{"type":"text","timestamp":1778895634268,"sessionID":"ses_1d19089d8ffeV9jPOAKa78KcAS","part":{"id":"prt_e2e713f40001QjiBDdEGUB2H7s","messageID":"msg_e2e703b82001SBAGJ134J3oaiP","sessionID":"ses_1d19089d8ffeV9jPOAKa78KcAS","type":"text","text":"I’ve settled on a timing-first structural hypothesis: turn IF into a real registered cutpoint so the live fetch/decode chain stops burning Fmax. I’m writing the YAML now.","time":{"start":1778895634240,"end":1778895634263},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0e4aa29cdb0f3cbd016a07cb1213788199aaf274835c4d7e6d","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778895635001,"sessionID":"ses_1d19089d8ffeV9jPOAKa78KcAS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_hUGxaBVCNJu9Zty19TEOYGrz","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\n+title: \"Registered Fetch/Decode Cutpoint\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current IF stage hands live instruction data straight into decode, so\n+  the fetch, decode, immediate generation, and regfile-read path stays on the\n+  FPGA timing critical path every cycle. A real registered cutpoint should\n+  shorten that combinational chain and raise Fmax without changing the in-order\n+  retirement model.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Convert IF into a true registered stage that latches {pc, instr, valid} on\n+  the clock edge and feeds ID from that register instead of directly from\n+  io_imemData. Keep the existing stall, flush, and redirect behavior intact so\n+  the architectural interface stays the same, but remove the live fetch-to-\n+  decode combinational dependency that likely limits median clock on Tang Nano\n+  20K. The expected win is higher Fmax with no change to RVFI ordering or ISA\n+  behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Insert a real IF/ID register and make decode consume the registered bundle instead of the live imem output.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypothe