{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899466886,"sessionID":"ses_1d155f15fffeXP5Dd3zHWfAReN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_yq0lZ0ZWQXoHExpPGqMP6f21","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r2s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\n+title: \"Precompute PC-relative targets\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\n+  though branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\n+  immediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\n+  critical path without changing architectural behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Precompute pc+imm in ID and carry that registered target through the pipeline\n+  so EX can reuse it for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/JAL instead of redoing the adder on\n+  the retire-critical path. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and all\n+  trap/redirect rules unchanged. This should trim the EX-stage timing cone with\n+  little area cost and recover some Fmax on CoreMark's call/branch-heavy mix.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decode and latch it with the rest of the ID/EX payload.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use the precomputed PC-relative target for branches and JAL, leaving only JALR target formation in EX.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r2s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r2s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r2s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r2s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\n+title: \"Precompute PC-relative targets\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\n+  though branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\n+  immediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\n+  critical path without changing architectural behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Precompute pc+imm in ID and carry that registered target through the pipeline\n+  so EX can reuse it for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/JAL instead of redoing the adder on\n+  the retire-critical path. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and all\n+  trap/redirect rules unchanged. This should trim the EX-stage timing cone with\n+  little area cost and recover some Fmax on CoreMark's call/branch-heavy mix.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decode and latch it with the rest of the ID/EX payload.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Use the precomputed PC-relative target for branches and JAL, leaving only JALR target formation in EX.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r2s1.yaml","relative