{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778899412831,"sessionID":"ses_1d155f16effeESobqYr8Q16gXs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_vEy3qKyguxZ2Qf1BJmBvzlWy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\n+title: \"Tiny return stack\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\n+  backward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\n+  expensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a very small fetch-stage return-address stack in `if_stage.sv` and use\n+  it to predict JALR returns (JALR x0, x1/x5, 0) directly in fetch. Keep\n+  EX-stage redirects as the recovery path for non-return JALR and any\n+  mispredicts. This should remove a high-value class of control-flow bubbles\n+  with less timing risk than a broader branch predictor.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r2s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r2s