{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778903392728,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b7cbffekcJZQgp4R2pQ7Z","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_sUQwtLAUnD2oqzaCbvcDGZ7Q","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Source-use aware interlock\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n+  younger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\n+  bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\n+  compare path on the stall logic.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\n+  the load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\n+  This should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\n+  trimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Source-use aware interlock\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n+  younger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\n+  bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\n+  compare path on the stall logic.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\n+  the load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\n+  This should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\n+  trimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Source-use aware interlock\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n+  younger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\n+  bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\n+  compare path on the stall logic.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\n+  the load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\n+  This should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\n+  trimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"\n","additions":25,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778903392708,"end":1778903392720}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0613ee53585e71d3016a07e95ec7fc8