n-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the generic load-data shifter in `mem_stage.sv` with a small\\nbyte/halfword select tree that extracts the requested lane directly from the\\nmemory word and only applies sign/zero extension for actual load widths.\\nKeep store masking and RVFI reporting unchanged. The goal is to trim the\\ncombinational depth on load-use cycles, which should raise median Fmax on\\nTang Nano 20K with no ISA-visible tradeoff.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 265.62, \"delta_pct\": -14.58, \"vs_baseline\": -6.08, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4949188, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10272, \"ff\": 1926, \"seeds\": [119.85, 143.18, 131.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, ...","metadata":{"matches":5,"truncated":false},"title":"micro_opt","time":{"start":1778913022293,"end":1778913022348}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a790cce497bfaa7016a080efe1b44819a979f37456e10a707"}},"id":"prt_e2f7a91500019QXyh9eXDrQ7Xo","sessionID":"ses_1d086a83cffe9kK36xLwk7ZrU7","messageID":"msg_e2f7a58ae001THsyrWDbBWWmd9"}}
