": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolve\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\\ncompare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\\nJALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\\nuntouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\\nCoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branches early and emit the exact redirect target for taken cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the ID-stage redirect into fetch and keep EX as the fallback path for JALR and recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"desc...\n  Line 12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split decode from read\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction decode and immediate/control extraction into the fetch-side\\nregistered bundle, then let ID focus on operand reads and latching only the\\nalready-predecoded metadata. This should shorten the ID-stage combinational\\npath and reduce fanout from the instruction bits while keeping stall, flush,\\nredirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded bundle directly so ID only performs regfile reads and state capture.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": ...","metadata":{"matches":5,"truncated":false},"title":"operand|source-use|source-aware|usage bits|forwarding select|compare path","time":{"start":1778913022286,"end":1778913022359}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a790cce497bfaa7016a080efe1b38819a93787039f44fcd91"}},"id":"prt_e2f7a911b00145THaFnnsd10Ue","sessionID":"ses_1d086a83cffe9kK36xLwk7ZrU7","messageID":"msg_e2f7a58ae001THsyrWDbBWWmd9"}}
