{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778913151759,"sessionID":"ses_1d086a83cffe9kK36xLwk7ZrU7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_f4yEtrzZOLsOC4wwA7PJhg1r","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\n+title: \"Source-aware operand gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\n+  live operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\n+  That keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\n+  can inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\n+  so load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n+  readers. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\n+  dead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\n+  This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while also helping Fmax.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add the usage sideband to the pipeline bundle so it can move with the instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction and expose them downstream.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits to avoid false stalls on payload-only operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares in EX forwarding selection.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\n+title: \"Source-aware operand gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\n+  live operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\n+  That keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\n+  can inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\n+  so load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n+  readers. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\n+  dead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\n+  This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while also helping Fmax.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add the usage sideband to the pipeline bundle so it can move with the instruction.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction and expose them downstream.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits to avoid false stalls on payload-only operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares in EX forwarding selection.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r5s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\n+title: \"Source-aware operand gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\n+  live operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\n+  That keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\n+  can inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\n+  so load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n+  readers. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\n+  dead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\n