{"type":"text","timestamp":1778914326642,"sessionID":"ses_1d0725296ffe04hte1OIgK20rq","part":{"id":"prt_e2f8e7801001XConygkVnFAe6Q","messageID":"msg_e2f8dd151001qY5UBLM32t70lh","sessionID":"ses_1d0725296ffe04hte1OIgK20rq","type":"text","text":"I’ve narrowed it to a smaller hazard-path optimization: classify whether the younger instruction actually reads rs1/rs2 before doing the load-use compare. I’m checking the hypothesis directory shape, then I’ll write the YAML.","time":{"start":1778914326529,"end":1778914326639},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0d1cf4848875d0b6016a0814164a0c819aaa2557a6c7515fd6","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778914326755,"sessionID":"ses_1d0725296ffe04hte1OIgK20rq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ZPMk6tNRFLlLgaXfCzuZntXJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","offset":1,"limit":30},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"id\": \"baseline-bench-adc6853\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T01:38:12.824520Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Gate false load-use stalls\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard check treats both raw IF/ID register fields as live sources,\\neven when the decoded instruction does not actually read rs2. That can inject\\navoidable one-cycle bubbles on immediate, jump, fence, and system instructions.\\nRemoving those false stalls should raise CoreMark IPC without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard check treats both raw IF/ID register fields as live sources,\\neven when the decoded instruction does not actually read rs2. That can inject\\navoidable one-cycle bubbles on immediate, jump, fence, and system instructions.\\nRemoving those false stalls should raise CoreMark IPC without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add source-usage awareness to load-use detection so only instructions that\\ntruly consume rs1/rs2 participate in the dependency compare. Keep the existing\\nstall/flush rules, but stop stalling on encodings whose rs2 bits are just\\nimmediate payload. This should recover wasted cycles in branch- and immediate-\\nheavy CoreMark code with minimal RTL risk.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass decoded instruction context into the hazard path so dependency checks can distinguish real operands from immediate fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage information and remove false bubbles for instructions that do not actually read rs2.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass decoded instruction context into the hazard path so dependency checks can distinguish real operands from immediate fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage information and remove false bubbles for instructions th... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Registered Fetch/Decode Cutpoint\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current IF stage hands live instruction data straight into decode, so\\nthe fetch, decode, immediate generation, and regfile-read path stays on the\\nFPGA timing critical path every cycle. A real registered cutpoint should\\nshorten that combinational chain and raise Fmax without changing the in-order\\nretirement model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current IF stage hands live instruction data straight into decode, so\\nthe fetch, decode, immediate generation, and regfile-read path stays on the\\nFPGA timing critical path every cycle. A real registered cutpoint should\\nshorten that combinational chain and raise Fmax without changing the in-order\\nretirement model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Convert IF into a true registered stage that latches {pc, instr, valid} on\\nthe clock edge and feeds ID from that register instead of directly from\\nio_imemData. Keep the existing stall, flush, and redirect behavior intact so\\nthe architectural interface stays the same, but remove the live fetch-to-\\ndecode combinational dependency that likely limits median clock on Tang Nano\\n20K. The expected win is higher Fmax with no change to RVFI ordering or ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Insert a real IF/ID register and make decode consume the registered bundle instead of the live imem output.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Insert a real IF/ID register and make decode consume the registered bundle instead of the live imem output.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 310.94, \"delta_pct\": 9.94, \"vs_baseline\": 9.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 153.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4949188, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9995, \"ff\": 1924, \"seeds\": [155.3, 144.49, 153.89], \"formal_pass... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static backward branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops and call-heavy control flow.\\nThe current core always waits for EX to resolve taken branches, so every\\ncorrectly taken loop branch pays the full redirect bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops and call-heavy control flow.\\nThe current core always waits for EX to resolve taken branches, so every\\ncorrectly taken loop branch pays the full redirect bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny fetch-stage predictor in `if_stage.sv` that predecodes the\\ncurrent instruction, predicts backward conditional branches and JAL as\\ntaken, and feeds the predicted target into the PC register immediately.\\nKeep EX-stage redirects as the recovery path for JALR and any mispredicts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a low-cost static predictor that computes branch/JAL targets in fetch and steers the PC before EX resolves the control flow.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a low-cost static predictor that computes branch/JAL targets in fetch and steers the PC before EX resolves the control flow.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 306.27, \"delta_pct\": 8.29, \"vs_baseline\": 8.29, \"fmax_mhz\": 130.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9969, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [126.65, 130.46, 130.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T02:41:20.069705Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.29%): Static backward-branch/JAL prediction is too blunt for CoreMark when EX still owns JALR and mispredict recovery, because the extra fetch-side logic on... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n5: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware load-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current interlock compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\ninstruction does not really consume that operand. That can insert avoidable\\nbubbles after loads on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it also\\nkeeps unnecessary compare logic on the stall path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current interlock compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\ninstruction does not really consume that operand. That can insert avoidable\\nbubbles after loads on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it also\\nkeeps unnecessary compare logic on the stall path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and feed them into the load-use\\ninterlock so the dependency check only fires when the younger instruction\\ntruly reads that source. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged,\\nbut stop stalling on payload-only register fields and trim the control-path\\nfanout that currently reaches the PC and IF/ID hold logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits alongside the decoded instruction bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the usage sideband into the interlock path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage information and remove false stalls on instructions that do not read the loaded operand.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute PC-relative targets\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute pc+imm in ID and carry that registered target through the pipeline\\nso EX can reuse it for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/JAL instead of redoing the adder on\\nthe retire-critical path. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and all\\ntrap/redirect rules unchanged. This should trim the EX-stage timing cone with\\nlittle area cost and recover some Fmax on CoreMark's call/branch-heavy mix.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decode and latch it with the rest of the ID/EX payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the precomputed PC-relative target for branches and JAL, leaving only JALR target formation in EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decod... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny return stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small fetch-stage return-address stack in `if_stage.sv` and use\\nit to predict JALR returns (JALR x0, x1/x5, 0) directly in fetch. Keep\\nEX-stage redirects as the recovery path for non-return JALR and any\\nmispredicts. This should remove a high-value class of control-flow bubbles\\nwith less timing risk than a broader branch predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 283.5, \"delta_pct\": -8.82, \"vs_baseline\": 0.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.02, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4938989, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10613, \"ff\": 2124, \"seeds\": [140.02, 139.57, 151.91], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T03:47:21.033640Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Source-use aware interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\\nbubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\\ncompare path on the stall logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\\nbubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\\ncompare path on the stall logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\\nthe load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\\nThis should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\\ntrimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolve\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\\ncompare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\\nJALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\\nuntouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\\nCoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branches early and emit the exact redirect target for taken cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the ID-stage redirect into fetch and keep EX as the fallback path for JALR and recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"desc... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\\nsaturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\\nJAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\\nwhen a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\\nthan the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\\nenough to avoid another Fmax regression.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.34, \"delta_pct\": -0.84, \"vs_baseline\": 9.02, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.91, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4407728, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10799, \"ff\": 2518, \"seeds\":... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n11: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Fast-path load extract\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Load retirement currently pays for a generic variable right-shift and\\nsign-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Load retirement currently pays for a generic variable right-shift and\\nsign-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the generic load-data shifter in `mem_stage.sv` with a small\\nbyte/halfword select tree that extracts the requested lane directly from the\\nmemory word and only applies sign/zero extension for actual load widths.\\nKeep store masking and RVFI reporting unchanged. The goal is to trim the\\ncombinational depth on load-use cycles, which should raise median Fmax on\\nTang Nano 20K with no ISA-visible tradeoff.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 265.62, \"delta_pct\": -14.58, \"vs_baseline\": -6.08, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4949188, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10272, \"ff\": 1926, \"seeds\": [119.85, 143.18, 131.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split decode from read\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction decode and immediate/control extraction into the fetch-side\\nregistered bundle, then let ID focus on operand reads and latching only the\\nalready-predecoded metadata. This should shorten the ID-stage combinational\\npath and reduce fanout from the instruction bits while keeping stall, flush,\\nredirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded bundle directly so ID only performs regfile reads and state capture.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Tagged loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow time in a few hot loops.\\nThe prior static and broad tiny-predictor ideas paid too much in aliasing,\\nwrong-target recovery, and fetch-side logic, which offset their IPC gains.\\nA narrower predictor that specializes in repeated loop backedges should\\ncapture the same common-case wins with less churn.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow time in a few hot loops.\\nThe prior static and broad tiny-predictor ideas paid too much in aliasing,\\nwrong-target recovery, and fetch-side logic, which offset their IPC gains.\\nA narrower predictor that specializes in repeated loop backedges should\\ncapture the same common-case wins with less churn.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small tagged loop predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that learns the\\ntaken count and exit point for the hottest backward conditional branch, then\\nspeculates that loop until the learned exit. Keep JALR and all cold branches\\nreactive in EX, and do not add a general BTB/BHT or return stack. This should\\nrecover the loop bodies CoreMark repeats most often while avoiding the aliasing\\nand bookkeeping that hurt prior predictor