n the stall logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\\nthe load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\\nThis should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\\ntrimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolve\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\\ncompare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\\nJALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\\nuntouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\\nCoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branches early and emit the exact redirect target for taken cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the ID-stage redirect into fetch and keep EX as the fallback path for JALR and recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"desc... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\\nsaturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\\nJAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\\nwhen a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\\nthan the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\\nenough to avoid another Fmax regression.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.34, \"delta_pct\": -0.84, \"vs_baseline\": 9.02, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.91, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4407728, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10799, \"ff\": 2518, \"seeds\":... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Fast-path load extract\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Load retirement currently pays for a generic variable right-shift and\\nsign-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Load retirement currently pays for a generic variable right-shift and\\nsign-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the generic load-data shifter in `mem_stage.sv` with a small\\nbyte/halfword select tree that extracts the requested lane directly from the\\nmemory word and only applies sign/zero extension for actual load widths.\\nKeep store masking and RVFI reporting unchanged. The goal is to trim the\\ncombinational depth on load-use cycles, which should raise median Fmax on\\nTang Nano 20K with no ISA-visible tradeoff.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 265.62, \"delta_pct\": -14.58, \"vs_baseline\": -6.08, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4949188, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10272, \"ff\": 1926, \"seeds\": [119.85, 143.18, 131.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split decode from read\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction decode and immediate/control extraction into the fetch-side\\nregistered bundle, then let ID focus on operand reads and latching only the\\nalready-predecoded metadata. This should shorten the ID-stage combinational\\npath and reduce fanout from the instruction bits while keeping stall, flush,\\nredirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded bundle directly so ID only performs regfile reads and state capture.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Tagged loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow time in a few hot loops.\\nThe prior static and broad tiny-predictor ideas paid too much in aliasing,\\nwrong-target recovery, and fetch-side logic, which offset their IPC gains.\\nA narrower predictor that specializes in repeated loop backedges should\\ncapture the same common-case wins with less churn.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow time in a few hot loops.\\nThe prior static and broad tiny-predictor ideas paid too much in aliasing,\\nwrong-target recovery, and fetch-side logic, which offset their IPC gains.\\nA narrower predictor that specializes in repeated loop backedges should\\ncapture the same common-case wins with less churn.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small tagged loop predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that learns the\\ntaken count and exit point for the hottest backward conditional branch, then\\nspeculates that loop until the learned exit. Keep JALR and all cold branches\\nreactive in EX, and do not add a general BTB/BHT or return stack. This should\\nrecover the loop bodies CoreMark repeats most often while avoiding the aliasing\\nand bookkeeping that hurt prior predictor attempts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches, learn a loop trip count from resolved outcomes, and steer fetch only for the hottest loop backedge.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches, learn a loop trip count from resolved outcomes, and steer fetch only for the hottest loop backedge.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 310.94, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 9.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 15... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware operand gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\\nlive operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\\nThat keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\\ncan inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\\nlive operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\\nThat keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\\ncan inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\\nso load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\\nreaders. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\\ndead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\\nThis should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while also helping Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the usage sideband to the pipeline bundle so it can move with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction and expose them downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits to avoid false stalls on payload-only operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares in EX forward... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\\nretirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\\ncombinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selec