 gating\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n  younger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\n  one-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\n  keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny operand-usage classifier inside the hazard unit so load-use stalls\n  only fire when the younger instruction really reads the compared source. Keep\n  forwarding, RVFI reporting, and the rest of the pipeline unchanged; only the\n  false dependency check should disappear. This should recover wasted CoreMark\n  cycles on payload-only register encodings with very low RTL risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r6s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778914340940,"end":1778914341013}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04958b4dc2987151016a08142498a0819b8423c45f15af178c"}},"id":"prt_e2f8eaf7f001wmLXlEbf4P634S","sessionID":"ses_1d0725296ffe04hte1OIgK20rq","messageID":"msg_e2f8ea2e1001DwKIAkTjvT1DN7"}}
