{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778934548806,"sessionID":"ses_1cf3dfcf9ffeG3N333ZuxwJsh3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_bA48CcM1hmDJZsBz3YDgVOtn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\n+title: \"Operand-usage hazard trim\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\n+  even when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\n+  That leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\n+  inject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decode-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\n+  load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\n+  Keep RVFI source snapshots and retirement behavior unchanged; only suppress\n+  dead compares and false stalls on instructions whose register fields are just\n+  immediate payload. This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while\n+  slightly shortening the hot hazard cone.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which instruction forms really read rs1 and rs2, alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream hazard logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares when an instruction does not read that source.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r9s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\n+title: \"Operand-usage hazard trim\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\n+  even when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\n+  That leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\n+  inject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decode-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\n+  load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\n+  Keep RVFI source snapshots and retirement behavior unchanged; only suppress\n+  dead compares and false stalls on instructions whose register fields are just\n+  immediate payload. This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while\n+  slightly shortening the hot hazard cone.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - fil