fields even when the\\ninstruction does not really consume that operand. That can insert avoidable\\nbubbles after loads on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it also\\nkeeps unnecessary compare logic on the stall path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and feed them into the load-use\\ninterlock so the dependency check only fires when the younger instruction\\ntruly reads that source. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged,\\nbut stop stalling on payload-only register fields and trim the control-path\\nfanout that currently reaches the PC and IF/ID hold logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits alongside the decoded instruction bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the usage sideband into the interlock path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage information and remove false stalls on instructions that do not read the loaded operand.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute PC-relative targets\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute pc+imm in ID and carry that registered target through the pipeline\\nso EX can reuse it for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/JAL instead of redoing the adder on\\nthe retire-critical path. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and all\\ntrap/redirect rules unchanged. This should trim the EX-stage timing cone with\\nlittle area cost and recover some Fmax on CoreMark's call/branch-heavy mix.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decode and latch it with the rest of the ID/EX payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the precomputed PC-relative target for branches and JAL, leaving only JALR target formation in EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decod... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny return stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small fetch-stage return-address stack in `if_stage.sv` and use\\nit to predict JALR returns (JALR x0, x1/x5, 0) directly in fetch. Keep\\nEX-stage redirects as the recovery path for non-return JALR and any\\nmispredicts. This should remove a high-value class of control-flow bubbles\\nwith less timing risk than a broader branch predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 283.5, \"delta_pct\": -8.82, \"vs_baseline\": 0.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.02, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4938989, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10613, \"ff\": 2124, \"seeds\": [140.02, 139.57, 151.91], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T03:47:21.033640Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 7 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview