{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778903427015,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b880ffeA5NVwid0iCtCqJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5pZws0YdaI0GV758YiKZ2HVH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\n2: title: \"Source-use aware interlock\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n6:   younger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\n7:   bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\n8:   compare path on the stall logic.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\n11:   the load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\n12:   This should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\n13:   trimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\n14: expected_impact:\n15:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n16:   confidence: medium\n17: changes:\n18:   - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n19:     description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n20:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n21:     description: \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n23:     description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n25:     description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Source-use aware interlock\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\n  younger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\n  bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\n  compare path on the stall logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\n  the load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\n  This should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\n  trimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r3s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778903426992,"end":1778903427014}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e31c3a6757a21dd016a07e982df9881989d3068eb20508775"}},"id":"prt_e2ee827a2001dU7RB3ALef1ChV","sessionID":"ses_1d119b880ffeA5NVwid0iCtCqJ","messageID":"msg_e2ee8130c001d2y9ZwzFy5QTJq"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778903427017,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b880ffeA5NVwid0iCtCqJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_HRYvz9lgZx958TDWBQGwTLiO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r3s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r3s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\n2: title: \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\n6:   redirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\n7:   prior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\n8:   control-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\n9:   behavior instead of assuming it.\n10: hypothesis: |\n11:   Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\n12:   saturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\n13:   JAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\n14:   when a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\n15:   than the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\n16:   enough to avoid another Fmax regression.\n17: expected_impact:\n18:   fitness_delta_pct: 6\n19:   confidence: medium\n20: changes:\n21:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\n  redirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\n  prior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\n  control-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\n  behavior instead of assuming it.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\n  saturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\n  JAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\n  when a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\n  than the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\n  enough to avoid another Fmax regression.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r3s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778903426995,"end":1778903427016}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e31c3a6757a21dd016a07e982dfb081988f0b16ca86e508fe"}},"id":"prt_e2ee827b2001hPDFl3SJseoTZB","sessionID":"ses_1d119b880ffeA5NVwid0iCtCqJ","messageID":"msg_e2ee8130c001d2y9ZwzFy5QTJq"}}
