{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778903474371,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b880ffeA5NVwid0iCtCqJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_zp5fchMe7iWILVpLKVEWDmxX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r3s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Early branch resolve\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\n+  waits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\n+  the hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\n+  in the pipeline.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\n+  compare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\n+  JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\n+  untouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\n+  CoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Resolve conditional branches early and emit the exact redirect target for taken cases.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Route the ID-stage redirect into fetch and keep EX as the fallback path for JALR and recovery.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r3s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-ru