ption: \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Early branch resolve\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\n  waits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\n  the hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\n  in the pipeline.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\n  compare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\n  JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\n  untouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\n  CoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r3s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778903479190,"end":1778903479213}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0867ccfc5941fb41016a07e9b66b04819b9e164e78eedac53a"}},"id":"prt_e2ee8f36f001XnlCzwev9bXRSJ","sessionID":"ses_1d119b880ffeA5NVwid0iCtCqJ","messageID":"msg_e2ee8e2070015iQ5jtU0iru55s"}}
