{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778913028551,"sessionID":"ses_1d086a8d8ffeXzoGyi304yynhF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_8SBs5Q5o2QQYmwAMpEbamXKO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\n+title: \"Retimed forwarding cut\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\n+  every instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\n+  keeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\n+  settled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\n+  retirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\n+  combinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\n+title: \"Retimed forwarding cut\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\n+  every instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\n+  keeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\n+  settled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\n+  retirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\n+  combinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\n+title: \"Retimed forwarding cut\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\n+  every instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\n+  keeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\n+  settled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\n+  retirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\n+  combinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"\n","additions":22,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r5s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778913028533,"end":1778913028548}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_010997fcf8e694a6016a080f03845881998034dfadcebab7ba"}},"id":"prt_e2f7aa6220015x6Z0FS3org942","sessionID":"ses_1d086a8d8ffeXzoGyi304yynhF","messageID":"msg_e2f7a8