{"type":"text","timestamp":1778922969245,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","part":{"id":"prt_e301257cb001UdFJCt7m1UqB9Y","messageID":"msg_e30124549001h7mFWJSsfyvdYS","sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","type":"text","text":"I confirmed the hypotheses directory exists. I’m sampling an existing hypothesis file format so the new YAML matches the local conventions.","time":{"start":1778922969035,"end":1778922969243},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0824ba14b4635f4c016a0835d8dfa08199a1560d1255aa901b","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778922969419,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6OdJ2BWm5Z07kXk7kprjExNr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r7s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r7s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\n2: title: \"Opcode-aware interlock trim\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current load-use interlock still treats raw IF/ID register fields as live\n6:   operands, even when the younger instruction does not actually read them. That\n7:   creates avoidable bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings\n8:   while keeping a hot compare cone on the PC-hold path.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Teach the hazard unit to classify whether the younger instruction truly reads\n11:   rs1 or rs2 before it checks the load-use dependency. By gating the compare on\n12:   real operand usage, the core should stop stalling on payload-only register\n13:   fields and slightly reduce stall-path fanout, improving CoreMark iter/cycle\n14:   without changing architectural behavior.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n20:     description: \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction into the hazard path so the interlock can classify operand usage locally.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n22:     description: \"Decode rs1/rs2 usage from opcode and funct fields, then gate load-use stalls so only true operand readers can trigger them.\"\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Opcode-aware interlock trim\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current load-use interlock still treats raw IF/ID register fields as live\n  operands, even when the younger instruction does not actually read them. That\n  creates avoidable bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings\n  while keeping a hot compare cone on the PC-hold path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Teach the hazard unit to classify whether the younger instruction truly reads\n  rs1 or rs2 before it checks the load-use dependency. By gating the compare on\n  real operand usage, the core should stop stalling on payload-only register\n  fields and slightly reduce stall-path fanout, improving CoreMark iter/cycle\n  without changing architectural behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction into the hazard path so the interlock can classify operand usage locally.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-001-r7s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778922969262,"end":1778922969418}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0824ba14b4635f4c016a0835d923a481999d4e734d0fe8e297"}},"id":"prt_e3012589e001wIoxjrKDKCNEcF","sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","messageID":"msg_e30124549001h7mFWJSsfyvdYS"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778922969439,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PGvcFqjnXTETNtY5slWjXKHF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\n2: title: \"Backward-only branch predictor\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\n6:   predictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\n7:   A narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\n8:   should keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\n9:   taken-branch bubbles.\n10: hypothesis: |\n11:   Add a tiny fetch-side predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that only predicts\n12:   backward conditional branches as taken, using a small counter table keyed by\n13:   PC bits and a locally computed `pc+imm` target. Leave JAL and JALR fully\n14:   reactive in EX, and keep mispredict recovery unchanged. This should avoid the\n15:   call/return churn and aliasing that hurt broader predictor variants while\n16:   still accelerating the loop-heavy paths CoreMark repeats most often.\n17: expected_impact:\n18:   fitness_delta_pct: 3\n19:   confidence: medium\n20: changes:\n21:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Add a small backward-branch-only predictor, steer fetch on hot taken loop branches, and leave JAL/JALR recovery in EX.\"\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Backward-only branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\n  predictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\n  A narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\n  should keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\n  taken-branch bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny fetch-side predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that only predicts\n  backward conditional branches as taken, using a small counter table keyed by\n  PC bits and a locally computed `pc+imm` target. Leave JAL and JALR fully\n  reactive in EX, and keep mispredict recovery unchanged. This should avoid the\n  call/return churn and aliasing that hurt broader predictor variants while\n  still accelerating the loop-heavy paths CoreMark repeats most often.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778922969384,"end":1778922969437}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0824ba14b4635f4c016a0835d923c481999a807d1db5dac4bb"}},"id":"prt_e301258b4001Z1XbzDQK00I5by","sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","messageID":"msg_e30124549001h7mFWJSsfyvdYS"}}
