{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778922980058,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Oyaz0gJFsCbhqiRyJs6DVrxw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.log","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.log</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778914276968,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8db665001P1K958266wb4w6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dafdf001hmcfk5QDkZegAQ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"snapshot\":\"3c8a7a8020e9dca93a57142c8f413102e396db8c\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n2: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778914280272,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8dc19c001arz12y7WQoC1bj\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dafdf001hmcfk5QDkZegAQ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Checking the prior predictor attempts and lessons first, then I’ll write a new hypothesis with the narrowest likely win.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778914279836,\"end\":1778914280260},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0f592ca7f26353fb016a0813e7ac70819b9e707b0605bac536\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778914280459,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_lPeTYwW3U0D0LFqfT7xd4pJi\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"hyp-20260516-.*predictor|predictor|branch|BTB|BHT|return stack\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 9 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Gate false load-use stalls\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current hazard check treats both raw IF/ID register fields as live sources,\\\\neven when the decoded instruction does not actually read rs2. That can inject\\\\navoidable one-cycle bubbles on immediate, jump, fence, and system instructions.\\\\nRemoving those false stalls should raise CoreMark IPC without changing ISA behavior.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current hazard check treats both raw IF/ID register fields as live sources,\\\\neven when the decoded instruction does not actually read rs2. That can inject\\\\navoidable one-cycle bubbles on immediate, jump, fence, and system instructions.\\\\nRemoving those false stalls should raise CoreMark IPC without changing ISA behavior.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add source-usage awareness to load-use detection so only instructions that\\\\ntruly consume rs1/rs2 participate in the dependency compare. Keep the existing\\\\nstall/flush rules, but stop stalling on encodings whose rs2 bits are just\\\\nimmediate payload. This should recover wasted cycles in branch- and immediate-\\\\nheavy CoreMark code with minimal RTL risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pass decoded instruction context into the hazard path so dependency checks ca... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778914280483,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_h7WGGPVvcvqyD9jvEdxYJGpK\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (broken, n/a): Load-use interlocks should gate on decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits, because raw register-field compares can falsely stall immediates, jumps, fences, and system ops on payload-only operand bits.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r1s1 (improvement, +9.94%): Turning IF into a real registered IF/ID cutpoint raised Fmax by removing the live io_imemData-to-decode combinational chain, but the register has to own flush/redirect/bubble behavior so control-flow changes still land as NOPs.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.29%): Static backward-branch/JAL prediction is too blunt for CoreMark when EX still owns JALR and mispredict recovery, because the extra fetch-side logic only pays off if the benchmark is dominated by backedges rather than mixed call-heavy control flow.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (regression, -7.17%): Precomputing branch/JAL targets in ID only helps if the added pc+imm adder does not become part of the decode critical path, because this just moves the same control-flow cone upstream instead of shortening the end-to-end timing path.\\n5: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays aligned with the benchmark's real call/return pattern; on CoreMark, the extra stack bookkeeping and redirect recovery can outweigh the bubbles saved on JALR returns.\\n6: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n5: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778914280670,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8dc4da001XcTu8mIem579Im\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"3c8a7a8020e9dca93a57142c8f413102e396db8c\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dafdf001hmcfk5QDkZegAQ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":38203,\"input\":22026,\"output\":196,\"reasoning\":109,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":15872}},\"cost\":0}}\n6: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778914281852,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8dc972001kGiprux9o3XPHe\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dc5b8001Uvy0IAlGybtAiX\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"snapshot\":\"3c8a7a8020e9dca93a57142c8f413102e396db8c\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n7: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778914298950,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8e0b8d001KzXkdOFEwG3a8n\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dc5b8001Uvy0IAlGybtAiX\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I’ve got the failure pattern: broad predictor state and extra bookkeeping have been hurting more than helping. I’m narrowing to a smaller, more targeted predictor with less aliasing and no extra recovery machinery.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778914298765,\"end\":1778914298945},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0e8f4f0050b1294a016a0813fa985c81998958b6d70e059fff\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n8: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778914299197,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"todowrite\",\"callID\":\"call_QXfSSjgLl306Pcoq5od6Pw0u\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Review prior predictor lessons and log history\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Draft the most promising predictor hypothesis for cores/bench\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Write the hypothesis YAML to cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"}]},\"output\":\"[\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Review prior predictor lessons and log history\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Draft the most promising predictor hypothesis for cores/bench\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Write the hypothesis YAML to cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  }\\n]\",\"metadata\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Review prior predictor lessons and log history\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Draft the most promising predictor hypothesis for cores/bench\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Write the hypothesis YAML to cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"}],\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"2 todos\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778914299191,\"end\":1778914299195}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_0e8f4f0050b1294a016a0813facb2c8199bfd63cc804e8c5c3\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2f8e0c46001eR1w30xu4mVJGk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dc5b8001Uvy0IAlGybtAiX\"}}\n9: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778914299458,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8e0e3c001I7wJjoghXAbXtq\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"3c8a7a8020e9dca93a57142c8f413102e396db8c\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8dc5b8001Uvy0IAlGybtAiX\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":45220,\"input\":5569,\"output\":135,\"reasoning\":1628,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":37888}},\"cost\":0}}\n10: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778914300845,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8e13a7001pRFVTZeMdnc6Un\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2f8e0f50001HTv1ghf0P51tkI\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251f5ffeB85JRWRTYUU5tY\",\