ply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_DiEIot8xuIZxCgwA9CFsVKGO\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\\n+title: \\\"Tagged 2-way branch predictor\\\"\\n+category: predictor\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The prior predictor attempts lost ground mostly to aliasing and fetch-side\\n+  bookkeeping, not because CoreMark lacks repeated control flow. A smaller but\\n+  better-indexed predictor should recover hot loop and call targets without the\\n+  wrong-target churn that hurt the direct-mapped BTB/BHT.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Replace the direct-mapped fetch predictor with a tiny 2-way tagged BTB/BHT in\\n+  `if_stage.sv`, using 2-bit counters and stored targets for taken conditional\\n+  branches and JAL while leaving JALR fully reactive in EX. The extra way and\\n+  tags should cut aliasing on CoreMark's small hot branch set, so the predictor\\n+  keeps its best entries alive without adding the deeper bookkeeping that hurt\\n+  the return-stack and loop-only variants.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Add a tiny 2-way tagged BTB/BHT, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches/JAL, and keep EX redirects as recovery for JALR and mispredicts.\\\"\\n*** End Patch\"},\"output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\",\"metadata\":{\"diff\":\"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\\n===================================================================\\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r6s2.yaml\\n+++ /Users/bo... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n21: {\"type\":\"step_fini