bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r6s1.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\\n+title: \\\"Retimed ID forwarding cut\\\"\\n+category: structural\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\n+  instruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\n+  the ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\n+  even after fetch was already registered.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\n+  settled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate copy\\n+  of the unforwarded source values for internal bookkeeping, while RVFI\\n+  continues to report the actual forwarded execution operands. This should\\n+  trim the EX-stage critical path and lower forwarding fanout without changing\\n+  ISA behavior or stall rules.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Route bypass selects and older-stage writeback values into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result, while preserving the raw regfile snapshot separately.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Drop the operand muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\\\"\\n*** End Patch\"},\"output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-0... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n31: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778914357885,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d07251c3ffeYWujJXZwFLWCpv\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2f8ef27b001wr05zAZvQJLMq8\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\