{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778923022420,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed19fffe9P8gu0tomAH3fh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_19BPqyKAIIJvzijLcIfo4beF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r7s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\n+title: \"Retimed operand bypass\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\n+  source compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\n+  compare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\n+  cycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\n+  settled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate raw\n+  source snapshot for bookkeeping, but have EX consume the already-selected\n+  operands directly so the bypass cone no longer sits on the ALU and branch\n+  critical path. This should shorten the retire path and raise Fmax without\n+  changing stall, flush, or RVFI semantics.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Split the operand fields so the pipeline can carry raw source reads separately from the settled execute operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Route bypass selects and writeback data into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result while preserving the raw regfile snapshot for bookkeeping.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Drop the per-operand bypass muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Upda