ut that currently reaches the PC and IF/ID hold logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits alongside the decoded instruction bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the usage sideband into the interlock path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage information and remove false stalls on instructions that do not read the loaded operand.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits so downstream logic can distinguish real operands from payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage ...\n  Line 6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute PC-relative targets\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute pc+imm in ID and carry that registered target through the pipeline\\nso EX can reuse it for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/JAL instead of redoing the adder on\\nthe retire-critical path. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and all\\ntrap/redirect rules unchanged. This should trim the EX-stage timing cone with\\nlittle area cost and recover some Fmax on CoreMark's call/branch-heavy mix.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decode and latch it with the rest of the ID/EX payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the precomputed PC-relative target for branches and JAL, leaving only JALR target formation in EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decod...\n  Line 7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny return stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small fetch-stage return-address stack in `if_stage.sv` and use\\nit to predict JALR returns (JALR x0, x1/x5, 0) directly in fetch. Keep\\nEX-stage redirects as the recovery path for non-return JALR and any\\nmispredicts. This should remove a high-value class of control-flow bubbles\\nwith less timing risk than a broader branch predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 283.5, \"delta_pct\": -8.82, \"vs_baseline\": 0.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.02, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4938989, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10613, \"ff\": 2124, \"seeds\": [140.02, 139.57, 151.91], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T03:47:21.033640Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays ...\n  Line 8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Source-use aware interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\\nbubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\\ncompare path on the stall logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use check compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read that source. That creates avoidable\\nbubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it keeps a hot\\ncompare path on the stall logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoded rs1/rs2 usage bits to the instruction decode path and feed them into\\nthe load-use interlock so the dependency check only fires on real operand reads.\\nThis should recover false stalls in CoreMark-heavy control flow while slightly\\ntrimming the hazard cone that reaches the PC hold logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits and stop stalling on payload-only register fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the usage bits out of decode so the stall path can see them.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard unit inputs.\"}, {\"file...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolve\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\\ncompare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\\nJALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\\nuntouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\\nCoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branches early and emit the exact redirect target for taken cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the ID-stage redirect into fetch and keep EX as the fallback path for JALR and recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"desc...\n  Line 10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\\nsaturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\\nJAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\\nwhen a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\\nthan the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\\nenough to avoid another Fmax regression.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.34, \"delta_pct\": -0.84, \"vs_baseline\": 9.02, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.91, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4407728, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10799, \"ff\": 2518, \"seeds\":...\n  Line 11: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Fast-path load extract\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Load retirement currently pays for a generic variable right-shift and\\nsign-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Load retirement currently pays for a generic variable right-shift and\\nsign-extension cone in the MEM stage, even though CoreMark's hot path is\\ndominated by simple word and byte accesses. Tightening that alignment logic\\nshould shorten the dmem->wb->forward path and improve Fmax without changing\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the generic load-data shifter in `mem_stage.sv` with a small\\nbyte/halfword select tree that extracts the requested lane directly from the\\nmemory word and only applies sign/zero extension for actual load widths.\\nKeep store masking and RVFI reporting unchanged. The goal is to trim the\\ncombinational depth on load-use cycles, which should raise median Fmax on\\nTang Nano 20K with no ISA-visible tradeoff.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable-shift load extraction path with direct byte/halfword selection and width-specific extension logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 265.62, \"delta_pct\": -14.58, \"vs_baseline\": -6.08, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4949188, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10272, \"ff\": 1926, \"seeds\": [119.85, 143.18, 131.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, ...\n  Line 12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split decode from read\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction decode and immediate/control extraction into the fetch-side\\nregistered bundle, then let ID focus on operand reads and latching only the\\nalready-predecoded metadata. This should shorten the ID-stage combinational\\npath and reduce fanout from the instruction bits while keeping stall, flush,\\nredirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded bundle directly so ID only performs regfile reads and state capture.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": ...\n  Line 13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Tagged loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow time in a few hot loops.\\nThe prior static and broad tiny-predictor ideas paid too much in aliasing,\\nwrong-target recovery, and fetch-side logic, which offset their IPC gains.\\nA narrower predictor that specializes in repeated loop backedges should\\ncapture the same common-case wins with less churn.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow time in a few hot loops.\\nThe prior static and broad tiny-predictor ideas paid too much in aliasing,\\nwrong-target recovery, and fetch-side logic, which offset their IPC gains.\\nA narrower predictor that specializes in repeated loop backedges should\\ncapture the same common-case wins with less churn.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small tagged loop predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that learns the\\ntaken count and exit point for the hottest backward conditional branch, then\\nspeculates that loop until the learned exit. Keep JALR and all cold branches\\nreactive in EX, and do not add a general BTB/BHT or return stack. This should\\nrecover the loop bodies CoreMark repeats most often while avoiding the aliasing\\nand bookkeeping that hurt prior predictor attempts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches, learn a loop trip count from resolved outcomes, and steer fetch only for the hottest loop backedge.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches, learn a loop trip count from resolved outcomes, and steer fetch only for the hottest loop backedge.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 310.94, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 9.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 15...\n  Line 14: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware operand gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\\nlive operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\\nThat keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\\ncan inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still treats raw register fields as\\nlive operands even when the decoded instruction does not actually read them.\\nThat keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\\ncan inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\\nso load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\\nreaders. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\\ndead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\\nThis should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while also helping Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the usage sideband to the pipeline bundle so it can move with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction and expose them downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits to avoid false stalls on payload-only operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares in EX forward...\n  Line 15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\\nretirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\\ncombinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume t...\n  Line 16: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"schema_error: while scanning a simple key\\n  in \\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\\\", line 7, column 1\\ncould not find expected ':'\\n  in \\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\\\", line 8, column 1\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5}\n\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-aware load-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\\nkeeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\\nkeeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny operand-usage classifier inside the hazard unit so load-use stalls\\nonly fire when the younger instruction really reads the compared source. Keep\\nforwarding, RVFI reporting, and the rest of the pipeline unchanged; only the\\nfalse dependency check should disappear. This should recover wasted CoreMark\\ncycles on payload-only register encodings with very low RTL risk.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify rs1/rs2 usage from opcode/funct fields and gate load-use compares so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify rs1/rs2 usage from opcode/funct fields and gate load-use compares so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_pas...\n  Line 18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed ID forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate copy\\nof the unforwarded source values for internal bookkeeping, while RVFI\\ncontinues to report the actual forwarded execution operands. This should\\ntrim the EX-stage critical path and lower forwarding fanout without changing\\nISA behavior or stall rules.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and older-stage writeback values into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result, while preserving the raw regfile snapshot separately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the operand muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description...\n  Line 19: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Tagged 2-way branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The prior predictor attempts lost ground mostly to aliasing and fetch-side\\nbookkeeping, not because CoreMark lacks repeated control flow. A smaller but\\nbetter-indexed predictor should recover hot loop and call targets without the\\nwrong-target churn that hurt the direct-mapped BTB/BHT.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The prior predictor attempts lost ground mostly to aliasing and fetch-side\\nbookkeeping, not because CoreMark lacks repeated control flow. A smaller but\\nbetter-indexed predictor should recover hot loop and call targets without the\\nwrong-target churn that hurt the direct-mapped BTB/BHT.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the direct-mapped fetch predictor with a tiny 2-way tagged BTB/BHT in\\n`if_stage.sv`, using 2-bit counters and stored targets for taken conditional\\nbranches and JAL while leaving JALR fully reactive in EX. The extra way and\\ntags should cut aliasing on CoreMark's small hot branch set, so the predictor\\nkeeps its best entries alive without adding the deeper bookkeeping that hurt\\nthe return-stack and loop-only variants.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny 2-way tagged BTB/BHT, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches/JAL, and keep EX redirects as recovery for JALR and mispredicts.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny 2-way tagged BTB/BHT, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches/JAL, and keep EX redirects as recovery for JALR and mispredicts.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: timeout\\nrun_all.sh exceeded 2700s wall-clock\\n--- partial output (tail) ---\\n8.6-198.31 step 20\\nSBY  5:24:49 [insn_bltu_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nSBY  5:25:01 [insn_sub_ch0] engine_0:...\n  Line 21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\\nsource compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\\ncompare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\\ncycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\\nsource compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\\ncompare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\\ncycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate raw\\nsource snapshot for bookkeeping, but have EX consume the already-selected\\noperands directly so the bypass cone no longer sits on the ALU and branch\\ncritical path. This should shorten the retire path and raise Fmax without\\nchanging stall, flush, or RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the operand fields so the pipeline can carry raw source reads separately from the settled execute operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and writeback data into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result while preserving the raw regfile snapshot for bookkeeping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand bypass muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the o...\n  Line 22: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Backward-only branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\\npredictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\\nA narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\\nshould keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\\ntaken-branch bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\\npredictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\\nA narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\\nshould keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\\ntaken-branch bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny fetch-side predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that only predicts\\nbackward conditional branches as taken, using a small counter table keyed by\\nPC bits and a locally computed `pc+imm` target. Leave JAL and JALR fully\\nreactive in EX, and keep mispredict recovery unchanged. This should avoid the\\ncall/return churn and aliasing that hurt broader predictor variants while\\nstill accelerating the loop-heavy paths CoreMark repeats most often.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small backward-branch-only predictor, steer fetch on hot taken loop branches, and leave JAL/JALR recovery in EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small backward-branch-only predictor, steer fetch on hot taken loop branches, and leave JAL/JALR recovery in EX.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: timeout\\nrun_all.sh exceeded 2700s wall-clock\\n--- partial output (tail) ---\\nclock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:06:11 (371)\\nSBY  7:2...","metadata":{"matches":20,"truncated":false},"title":"structural|predictor|branch|forward|retime|decode|fetch","time":{"start":1778929101015,"end":1778929101072}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_090e1e56fb9a30ef016a084dccbd38819ab421a1a3904437e6"}},"id":"prt_e306fe8cc001GVm6ZiwYcDThJ2","sessionID":"ses_1cf90384dffeR4pNp9jZSrmV8A","messageID":"msg_e306fcbcd00179UeEW5UE3VPak"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778929101255,"sessionID":"ses_1cf90384dffeR4pNp9jZSrmV8A","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Noc2KDf1cQ3ErJC09gnmo1EI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (broken, n/a): Load-use interlocks should gate on decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits, because raw register-field compares can falsely stall immediates, jumps, fences, and system ops on payload-only operand bits.\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r1s1 (improvement, +9.94%): Turning IF into a real registered IF/ID cutpoint raised Fmax by removing the live io_imemData-to-decode combinational chain, but the register has to own flush/redirect/bubble behavior so control-flow changes still land as NOPs.\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.29%): Static backward-branch/JAL prediction is too blunt for CoreMark when EX still owns JALR and mispredict recovery, because the extra fetch-side logic only pays off if the benchmark is dominated by backedges rather than mixed call-heavy control flow.\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (regression, -7.17%): Precomputing branch/JAL targets in ID only helps if the added pc+imm adder does not become part of the decode critical path, because this just moves the same control-flow cone upstream instead of shortening the end-to-end timing path.\n5: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays aligned with the benchmark's real call/return pattern; on CoreMark, the extra stack bookkeeping and redirect recovery can outweigh the bubbles saved on JALR returns.\n6: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): Early branch resolution in ID must reuse the same forwarding and stall discipline as EX, or stale compare operands will misdirect the PC and trip the formal pc_fwd/reg checks.\n7: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-003-r3s2 (regression, -0.84%): A learned predictor only beats the static backward guess if the BTB/BHT is large enough for CoreMark's hot branch footprint; a tiny direct-mapped table just adds aliasing and wrong-target churn to an already loop-heavy control flow.\n8: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-001-r4s0 (regression, -14.58%): Manually replacing a variable load-data shift with a byte/halfword lane-select tree can hurt Fmax if the original shift was not the true critical path, because the extra muxing and decode fanout outweigh the hoped-for cone reduction.\n9: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r4s1 (regression, -9.36%): Predecoding instruction fields in IF only helps if the fetch-side stage has slack to absorb the decoder and imm-gen cone; otherwise the work just moves the timing hotspot upstream and increases instruction-bit fanout without shortening the critical path.\n10: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r5s1 (broken, n/a): Moving bypass selection into ID only works if you keep the forwarded execute operands distinct from the raw regfile readbacks RVFI records; otherwise the core can retire with stale source-operand metadata even when the data path itself is functionally close.\n11: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A tiny tagged 2-way BTB/BHT only helps if the extra tag/way/LRU state still fits the formal timeout budget; once predictor bookkeeping becomes the heaviest part of the fetch cone, `run_all.sh` can stall before any CoreMark benefit is measurable.\n12: - 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r7s1 (regression, -16.15%): Retiming bypass muxing into ID can backfire if the added compare and forwarding fanout on decode is heavier than the ALU cone it removes, because the critical path just shifts upstream instead of getting shorter.\n\n(End of file - total 12 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (broken, n/a): Load-use interlocks should gate on decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits, because raw register-field compares can falsely stall immediates, jumps, fences, and system ops on payload-only operand bits.\n- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r1s1 (improvement, +9.94%): Turning IF into a real registered IF/ID cutpoint raised Fmax by removing the live io_imemData-to-decode combinational chain, but the register has to own flush/redirect/bubble behavior so control-flow changes still land as NOPs.\n- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.29%): Static backward-branch/JAL prediction is too blunt for CoreMark when EX still owns JALR and mispredict recovery, because the extra fetch-side logic only pays off if the benchmark is dominated by backedges rather than mixed call-heavy control flow.\n- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (regression, -7.17%): Precomputing branch/JAL targets in ID only helps if the added pc+imm adder does not become part of the decode critical path, because this just moves the same control-flow cone upstream instead of shortening the end-to-end timing path.\n- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays aligned with the benchmark's real call/return pattern; on CoreMark, the extra stack bookkeeping and redirect recovery can outweigh the bubbles saved on JALR returns.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): Early branch resolution in ID must reuse the same forwarding and stall discipline as EX, or stale compare operands will misdirect the PC and trip the formal pc_fwd/reg checks.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-003-r3s2 (regression, -0.84%): A learned predictor only beats the static backward guess if the BTB/BHT is large enough for CoreMark's hot branch footprint; a tiny direct-mapped table just adds aliasing and wrong-target churn to an already loop-heavy control flow.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-001-r4s0 (regression, -14.58%): Manually replacing a variable load-data shift with a byte/halfword lane-select tree can hurt Fmax if the original shift was not the true critical path, because the extra muxing and decode fanout outweigh the hoped-for cone reduction.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r4s1 (regression, -9.36%): Predecoding instruction fields in IF only helps if the fetch-side stage has slack to absorb the decoder and imm-gen cone; otherwise the work just moves the timing hotspot upstream and increases instruction-bit fanout without shortening the critical path.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r5s1 (broken, n/a): Moving bypass selection into ID only works if you keep the forwarded execute operands distinct from the raw regfile readbacks RVFI records; otherwise the core can retire with stale source-operand metadata even when the data path itself is functionally close.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A tiny tagged 2-way BTB/BHT only helps if the extra tag/way/LRU state still fits the formal timeout budget; once predictor bookkeeping becomes the heaviest part of the fetch cone, `run_all.sh` can stall before any CoreMark benefit is measurable.\n- 2026-05-16 hyp-20260516-002-r7s1 (regression, -16.15%): Retiming bypass muxing into ID can backfire if the added compare and forwarding fanout on decode is heavier than the ALU cone it removes, because the critical path just shifts upstream instead of getting shorter.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/LESSONS.md","time":{"start":1778929101000,"end":1778929101253}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_090e1e56fb9a30ef016a084dccbd28819abeade44f15eb6199"}},"id":"prt_e306fe8bc001OTDEqv4pMHkb6S","sessionID":"ses_1cf90384dffeR4pNp9jZSrmV8A","messageID":"msg_e306fcbcd00179UeEW5UE3VPak"}}
