ctually read them.\\nThat keeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX operand paths and\\ncan inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\\nso load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\\nreaders. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\\ndead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\\nThis should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while also helping Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the usage sideband to the pipeline bundle so it can move with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction and expose them downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits to avoid false stalls on payload-only operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares in EX forward...\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-aware load-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\\nkeeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\\nkeeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny operand-usage classifier inside the hazard unit so load-use stalls\\nonly fire when the younger instruction really reads the compared source. Keep\\nforwarding, RVFI reporting, and the rest of the pipeline unchanged; only the\\nfalse dependency check should disappear. This should recover wasted CoreMark\\ncycles on payload-only register encodings with very low RTL risk.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify rs1/rs2 usage from opcode/funct fields and gate load-use compares so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify rs1/rs2 usage from opcode/funct fields and gate load-use compares so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_pas...\n  Line 20: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-aware interlock trim\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use interlock still treats raw IF/ID register fields as live\\noperands, even when the younger instruction does not actually read them. That\\ncreates avoidable bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings\\nwhile keeping a hot compare cone on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use interlock still treats raw IF/ID register fields as live\\noperands, even when the younger instruction does not actually read them. That\\ncreates avoidable bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings\\nwhile keeping a hot compare cone on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Teach the hazard unit to classify whether the younger instruction truly reads\\nrs1 or rs2 before it checks the load-use dependency. By gating the compare on\\nreal operand usage, the core should stop stalling on payload-only register\\nfields and slightly reduce stall-path fanout, improving CoreMark iter/cycle\\nwithout changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction into the hazard path so the interlock can classify operand usage locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode rs1/rs2 usage from opcode and funct fields, then gate load-use stalls so only true operand readers can trigger them.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction into the hazard path so the interlock can classify operand usage locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode rs1/rs2 usage from opcode and funct fields, then gate load-use stalls so only true operand readers can trigger them.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_fai...\n  Line 22: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Backward-only branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\\npredictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\\nA narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\\nshould keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\\ntaken-branch bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\\npredictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\\nA narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\\nshould keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\\ntaken-branch bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny fetch-side predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that only predicts\\nbackward conditional branches as taken, using a small counter table keyed by\\nPC bits and a locally computed `pc+imm` target. Leave JAL and JALR fully\\nreactive in EX, and keep mispredict recovery unchanged. This should avoid the\\ncall/return churn and aliasing that hurt broader predictor variants while\\nstill accelerating the loop-heavy paths CoreMark repeats most often.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small backward-branch-only predictor, steer fetch on hot taken loop branches, and leave JAL/JALR recovery in EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small backward-branch-only predictor, steer fetch on hot taken loop branches, and leave JAL/JALR recovery in EX.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: timeout\\nrun_all.sh exceeded 2700s wall-clock\\n--- partial output (tail) ---\\nclock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:06:11 (371)\\nSBY  7:2...","metadata":{"matches":11,"truncated":false},"title":"imm_gen|immediate|imm\\b","time":{"start":1778929164301,"end":1778929164511}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0cfbebc