\ncan inject false stalls on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage flags and thread them through the pipeline\\nso load-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\\nreaders. Keep the retirement model and ISA behavior unchanged, but trim the\\ndead compare cone that currently feeds stall, mux select, and PC-hold logic.\\nThis should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while also helping Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits for each decoded instruction class.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the usage sideband to the pipeline bundle so it can move with the instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction and expose them downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage flags into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits to avoid false stalls on payload-only operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same source-usage bits to skip dead operand compares in EX forward...","metadata":{"matches":7,"truncated":false},"title":"predecode|predecoded|decode from read|decode.*imm","time":{"start":1778929164336,"end":1778929164535}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0cfbebc43489169c016a084e0c1644819a96f597bd3c9f420a"}},"id":"prt_e3070e01b0012MeGBVH8JCYvan","sessionID":"ses_1cf90384dffeR4pNp9jZSrmV8A","messageID":"msg_e3070a2c20017eMCBbVMClYdsM"}}
