{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778934517536,"sessionID":"ses_1cf3dfac7ffec6FBXuVzTW006u","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_e6IeHq6MefiNjmybEvFDhMei","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"MUL|DIV|divider|multiplier|M-extension|ALU","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 4 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolve\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark burns a lot of cycles on tight conditional loops, and this core still\\nwaits until EX to confirm taken branches. That leaves a full redirect bubble on\\nthe hot path even though the branch operands are already available much earlier\\nin the pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move exact resolution of BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU into ID with a dedicated\\ncompare-and-target path that uses the decoded operands before EX runs. Keep\\nJALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and leave the ALU and memory paths\\nuntouched. This should cut one cycle from the common taken-branch case on\\nCoreMark's loop-heavy control flow without adding speculative predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branches early and emit the exact redirect target for taken cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the ID-stage redirect into fetch and keep EX as the fallback path for JALR and recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain JAL/JALR and trap handling, but stop re-resolving conditional branches that ID already handled.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide branch-facing operand selection so the ID stage can compare the freshest rs1/rs2 values before EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"desc...\n  Line 15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\\nretirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\\ncombinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume t...\n  Line 18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed ID forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate copy\\nof the unforwarded source values for internal bookkeeping, while RVFI\\ncontinues to report the actual forwarded execution operands. This should\\ntrim the EX-stage critical path and lower forwarding fanout without changing\\nISA behavior or stall rules.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and older-stage writeback values into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result, while preserving the raw regfile snapshot separately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the operand muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description...\n  Line 21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\\nsource compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\\ncompare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\\ncycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\\nsource compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\\ncompare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\\ncycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate raw\\nsource snapshot for bookkeeping, but have EX consume the already-selected\\noperands directly so the bypass cone no longer sits on the ALU and branch\\ncritical path. This should shorten the retire path and raise Fmax without\\nchanging stall, flush, or RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the operand fields so the pipeline can carry raw source reads separately from the settled execute operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and writeback data into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result while preserving the raw regfile snapshot for bookkeeping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand bypass muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the o...","metadata":{"matches":4,"truncated":false},"title":"MUL|DIV|divider|multiplier|M-extension|ALU","time":{"start":1778934517423,"end":1778934517527}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ef9a538f05849b4016a0862f544d4819a84b8a77c13530b7f"}},"id":"prt_e30c28e83001H9b348IlY9tWxh","sessionID":"ses_1cf3dfac7ffec6FBXuVzTW006u","messageID":"msg_e30c22f88001qTTy1kigO8HUjf"}}
