{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778934546099,"sessionID":"ses_1cf3dfac7ffec6FBXuVzTW006u","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_CK69FNCAdRdPa6g5h6CVGZmb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\n+title: \"Split slow M-extension path\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\n+  combinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\n+  with the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\n+  core close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\n+  CoreMark.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Split the ALU into a fast single-cycle RV32I path and a separate slow RV32M\n+  backend for MUL/DIV/REM operations. Keep simple arithmetic, shifts, compares,\n+  and branch evaluation on the fast path, then stall the pipeline only while an\n+  M-operation is in flight and forward its finished result into writeback. This\n+  should remove the worst-case multiplier/divider cone from the retire-critical\n+  path without changing architectural results or RVFI-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from the slow RV32M multiply/divide path, with registered completion for M-ops.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch and consume the fast-path ALU result directly, while coordinating stalls and result capture for the slow M backend.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Treat an active M-operation as a stall condition so younger instructions wait for the slow result without corrupting retirement order.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-002-r9s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"I