{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1778903317785,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b854ffe1iv41ycFp5lzgs","part":{"id":"prt_e2ee67d14001Rc7cIXQWKhmzWg","messageID":"msg_e2ee6791b001TKMgoNyCjrS8T8","sessionID":"ses_1d119b854ffe1iv41ycFp5lzgs","snapshot":"3dd1dc0b19da65f1ae722cf190761885437659cc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1778903335656,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b854ffe1iv41ycFp5lzgs","part":{"id":"prt_e2ee6c291001MVruie9BJwyfsx","messageID":"msg_e2ee6791b001TKMgoNyCjrS8T8","sessionID":"ses_1d119b854ffe1iv41ycFp5lzgs","type":"text","text":"I’ve narrowed it to a tiny direct-mapped BTB plus 2-bit counters in fetch: enough to learn CoreMark’s hot loop branches, but narrower than the failed static predictor and RAS attempts. I’m writing that as the hypothesis now.","time":{"start":1778903335570,"end":1778903335655},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_046bc52e17035ab7016a07e92765d4819880d8225851ea73e2","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778903336742,"sessionID":"ses_1d119b854ffe1iv41ycFp5lzgs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_vtxcpWhpvdVQ9bChJR5ojGnN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r3s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\n+title: \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\n+  redirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\n+  prior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\n+  control-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\n+  behavior instead of assuming it.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\n+  saturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\n+  JAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\n+  when a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\n+  than the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\n+  enough to avoid another Fmax regression.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r3s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r3s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-2026051