{"type":"text","timestamp":1778913033008,"sessionID":"ses_1d086a74effeomxicsUahdYgYH","part":{"id":"prt_e2f7abae9001iEnQRDYLqJLbDx","messageID":"msg_e2f7a45b0001s7xkqEuRm6EQgV","sessionID":"ses_1d086a74effeomxicsUahdYgYH","type":"text","text":"I’ve got the hypothesis shape: keep predictor logic minimal, but drop JAL speculation so the fetch cone stays cheap and the call-heavy part of CoreMark doesn’t pay for a branch predictor it can’t use. Writing the YAML now.","time":{"start":1778913032937,"end":1778913033005},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_05999025d7acecae016a080f08cb4481988f88b12271eb8eb7","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778913033781,"sessionID":"ses_1d086a74effeomxicsUahdYgYH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_dxNlrFZr45Rxk5LHIaD6S7O7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r5s2\n+title: \"Branch-only BTFNT\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still leaves a lot of money on the table in tight backward loops,\n+  but the earlier predictor attempts paid too much for call-heavy control flow\n+and fetch-side complexity. A narrower predictor that only handles backward\n+conditional branches could keep the logic cheap enough to preserve Fmax while\n+still removing the most common taken-branch bubbles.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny fetch-stage predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that predicts only\n+  backward conditional branches as taken. Do not speculate JAL or JALR, and do\n+  not add a BTB, BHT, or return stack; keep EX-stage redirects as the recovery\n+  path for every miss. This should preserve the loop wins of static BTFNT while\n+  avoiding the extra fetch-side work that made the broader predictor variants\n+  regress.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a minimal backward-conditional-branch predictor in fetch, and keep direct JAL/JALR control-flow reactive in EX.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r5s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto