{"type":"text","timestamp":1778922943663,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed14dffe9ClxKakXBEKkHZ","part":{"id":"prt_e3011f493001cd14nXRe6t3LEc","messageID":"msg_e3011515e001WHqZPnjk4dlSSg","sessionID":"ses_1cfeed14dffe9ClxKakXBEKkHZ","type":"text","text":"I’ve narrowed it to a lighter branch-only predictor: skip JAL/JALR speculation entirely and keep the fetch logic narrow enough to avoid the earlier aliasing and bookkeeping regressions. Writing that as the new hypothesis now.","time":{"start":1778922943635,"end":1778922943659},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_070532c1d421616f016a0835bf76c481988e9c9e23f810a256","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778922944420,"sessionID":"ses_1cfeed14dffe9ClxKakXBEKkHZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_mwHWZMQdIXFA3UN2GbhrfUda","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r7s2\n+title: \"Backward-only branch predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark's hot control flow is dominated by loop backedges, but the prior\n+  predictor attempts spent too much logic on JAL/JALR and richer BTB/RAS state.\n+  A narrower predictor that only speculates on backward conditional branches\n+  should keep fetch-side timing simpler while still recovering the most common\n+  taken-branch bubbles.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny fetch-side predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that only predicts\n+  backward conditional branches as taken, using a small counter table keyed by\n+  PC bits and a locally computed `pc+imm` target. Leave JAL and JALR fully\n+  reactive in EX, and keep mispredict recovery unchanged. This should avoid the\n+  call/return churn and aliasing that hurt broader predictor variants while\n+  still accelerating the loop-heavy paths CoreMark repeats most often.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a small backward-branch-only predictor, steer fetch on hot taken loop branches, and leave JAL/JALR recovery in EX.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r7s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp