{"type":"text","timestamp":1778929131786,"sessionID":"ses_1cf90377fffevB5Js707coDIaL","part":{"id":"prt_e3070608e001zfbuhCVE650LDw","messageID":"msg_e306febe8001F079sbDF6j72ui","sessionID":"ses_1cf90377fffevB5Js707coDIaL","type":"text","text":"I’ve narrowed this to a very small predictor angle: a single-entry, learned loop/backedge cache instead of a wider BTB/RAS. I’m writing that as the hypothesis now.","time":{"start":1778929131662,"end":1778929131783},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0d993a275165f705016a084deb803881998e9787f9281d5e7b","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778929135062,"sessionID":"ses_1cf90377fffevB5Js707coDIaL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_HMbVVIUwOlgSNQA4Zu8i0MbM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r8s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260516-003-r8s2\n+title: \"Single-entry loop predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark keeps reusing a small number of hot backward branches, but the\n+  broader predictor experiments already showed that extra BTB/RAS state can\n+  erase the benefit through aliasing and fetch-side overhead. A very small\n+  predictor that only remembers one hot loop backedge should be cheaper to\n+  update and easier to time.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a single-entry learned predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that caches the\n+  target and taken direction for the hottest backward conditional branch, then\n+  steers fetch early when the same PC reappears. Do not add a general BTB, RAS,\n+  or JALR speculation; keep EX as the recovery path for everything else. This\n+  is narrower than the prior table-based attempts and should capture the\n+  repeat-backedge behavior CoreMark actually exercises without the bookkeeping\n+  that hurt Fmax.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a one-entry learned predictor for the hottest backward conditional branch and use it to redirect fetch before EX resolves the loop backedge.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r8s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260516-003-r8s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mi