{"type":"text","timestamp":1778990294746,"sessionID":"ses_1cbeac647ffej9KyVHDbMabJGj","part":{"id":"prt_e3415a6d8001UPAc7RZS0a401G","messageID":"msg_e341562a7001TIISu658HixZpG","sessionID":"ses_1cbeac647ffej9KyVHDbMabJGj","type":"text","text":"Writing the hypothesis now. I’m keeping it narrow: operand-usage gating for hazard/forward compares, not a topology change.","time":{"start":1778990294744,"end":1778990294745},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0d1328e07a101d06016a093cd689a88194999f28ddda506fe7","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778990296606,"sessionID":"ses_1cbeac647ffej9KyVHDbMabJGj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_vDIMfZxELPPTSqU9bwV1lLOV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Operand-usage gated compares\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core still spends timing budget comparing raw register fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not really read that operand. That creates dead\n+  compare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\n+  load-use stalls on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits, carry them through the pipeline, and\n+  use them to suppress hazard and forwarding compares for instructions that do\n+  not actually consume a source register. Keep the operand muxing, RVFI data,\n+  and retirement order unchanged; only the dead compare cone should disappear.\n+  This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles and trim the hot stall path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for unused sources so the EX forwarding cone is narrower on common immediates and jumps.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Operand-usage gated compares\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core still spends timing budget comparing raw register fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not really read that operand. That creates dead\n+  compare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\n+  load-use stalls on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits, carry them through the pipeline, and\n+  use them to suppress hazard and forwarding compares for instructions that do\n+  not actually consume a source register. Keep the operand muxing, RVFI data,\n+  and retirement order unchanged; only the dead compare cone should disappear.\n+  This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles and trim the hot stall path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for unused sources so the EX forwarding cone is narrower on common immediates and jumps.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Operand-usage gated compares\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core still spends timing budget comparing raw register fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not really read that operand. That creates dead\n+  compare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\n+  load-use stalls on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits, carry them through the pipeline, and\n+  use them to suppress hazard and forwarding compares for instructions that do\n+  not actually consume a source register. Keep the operand muxing, RVFI data,\n+  and retirement order unchanged; only the dead compare cone should disappear.\n+  This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles and trim the hot stall path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for unused sources so the EX forwarding cone is narrower on common immediates and jumps.\"\n","additions":30,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r10s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778990296603,"end":1778990296605}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d1328e07a101d06016a093cd69fe88194a27e997890ec3fd9"}},"id":"prt_e3415a6d9010Ri7L78SwczTIOk","sessionID":"ses_1cbeac647ffej9KyVHDbMabJGj","messageID":"msg_e341562a7001TIISu658HixZpG"}}
