{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778991439179,"sessionID":"ses_1cbd98f91ffecj5Hfn2H6yYcHz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_T1JOzLSDNzXAxhSUeSvMUpLT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r11s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n+  when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That leaves\n+  dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n+  stalls on immediate, jump, fence, and SYSTEM encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\n+  the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\n+  Keep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement ordering unchanged; only the\n+  dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear. This should\n+  recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the stall/forwarding path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead rs1/rs2 compares when the instruction does not actually consume that source, reducing fanout on the EX bypass path.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r11s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r11s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r11s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r11s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n+  when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That leaves\n+  dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n+  stalls on immediate, jump, fence, and SYSTEM encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\n+  the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\n+  Keep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement ordering unchanged; only the\n+  dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear. This should\n+  recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the stall/forwarding path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bund