{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778996237748,"sessionID":"ses_1cb905347ffeY45FPdLrmabthk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_bHJ8CHkkYA1cOUs9buAvQOma","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r12s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated hazard cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The hot hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not actually read them. That leaves dead compare\n+  fanout on the stall path and can also inject false load-use bubbles on payload-\n+  only encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's control-heavy mix.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n+  load-use detection and operand forwarding only fire for real source reads.\n+  Keep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged; the only\n+  architectural effect should be fewer false stalls and a shorter compare cone\n+  on the PC-hold / bypass paths.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/