{"type":"text","timestamp":1778998314263,"sessionID":"ses_1cb71120effeY0PpQwnrYZQ2Gl","part":{"id":"prt_e3490042e00160wdYUwnKuCCGg","messageID":"msg_e348fdae0001B0cTgrCnq8EVyT","sessionID":"ses_1cb71120effeY0PpQwnrYZQ2Gl","type":"text","text":"The hypothesis file will include the full sideband thread, but only for compare gating. I’m not changing retirement semantics or RVFI data flow.","time":{"start":1778998314030,"end":1778998314262},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_06efbee5a6ea4ac2016a095c29efc4819697b144744a296a26","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778998316315,"sessionID":"ses_1cb71120effeY0PpQwnrYZQ2Gl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_CDbEUTgTMOqpV91YiUEPxO7r","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core still spends timing budget comparing raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not actually read one of them. That leaves dead\n+  compare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\n+  load-use stalls on payload-only encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's\n+  control-heavy mix.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n+  load-use detection and operand forwarding only fire for real source reads.\n+  Keep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged; the only\n+  architectural effect should be fewer false stalls and a shorter compare cone\n+  on the PC-hold and bypass paths. This should recover a few CoreMark cycles\n+  while also trimming the hot hazard logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core still spends timing budget comparing raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not actually read one of them. That leaves dead\n+  compare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\n+  load-use stalls on payload-only encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's\n+  control-heavy mix.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n+  load-use detection and operand forwarding only fire for real source reads.\n+  Keep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged; the only\n+  architectural effect should be fewer false stalls and a shorter compare cone\n+  on the PC-hold and bypass paths. This should recover a few CoreMark cycles\n+  while also trimming the hot hazard logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r13s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The core still spends timing budget comparing raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\n+  the younger instruction does not actually read one of them. That leaves dead\n+  compare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject