from the synthesized combinational logic\\nwhile preserving the current architectural stall model for rare M-ops. The\\ncommon RV32I/CoreMark path should close timing more easily, and the extra\\ncycles on divide/remainder should be amortized by their low frequency.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/m_backend.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the registered M backend so MUL remains fast while DIV/REM use a tiny iterative state machine instead of a wide combinational divide cone.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/m_backend.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the registered M backend so MUL remains fast while DIV/REM use a tiny iterative state machine instead of a wide combinational divide cone.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"build_failed: yosys synth: ERROR: Latch inferred for signal `\\\\m_divider.\\\\rem_shift' from always_comb process `\\\\m_divider.$proc$cores/bench/rtl/m_divider.sv:52$187'.\",...","metadata":{"matches":5,"truncated":false},"title":"mem_stage|load-data|load extract|shift|byte/halfword","time":{"start":1779000053072,"end":1779000053086}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_001694099832e069016a0962f4e804819092d988b0d7233f97"}},"id":"prt_e34aa8d33001xnJoJzg7tR4Oal","sessionID":"ses_1cb55a92dffeMp9pGqGFVEfjKE","messageID":"msg_e34aa6b1c001QcbO6gQsLXhxGO"}}
