fetch and steers the PC before EX resolves the control flow.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 306.27, \"delta_pct\": 8.29, \"vs_baseline\": 8.29, \"fmax_mhz\": 130.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9969, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [126.65, 130.46, 130.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T02:41:20.069705Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.29%): Static backward-branch/JAL prediction is too blunt for CoreMark when EX still owns JALR and mispredict recovery, because the extra fetch-side logic on...\n  Line 6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute PC-relative targets\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage still spends timing budget on PC-relative target math even\\nthough branch and JAL destinations depend only on the already-decoded PC and\\nimmediate. Retiming that add out of EX should shorten the control-flow\\ncritical path without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute pc+imm in ID and carry that registered target through the pipeline\\nso EX can reuse it for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/JAL instead of redoing the adder on\\nthe retire-critical path. Keep JALR's rs1+imm calculation and all\\ntrap/redirect rules unchanged. This should trim the EX-stage timing cone with\\nlittle area cost and recover some Fmax on CoreMark's call/branch-heavy mix.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decode and latch it with the rest of the ID/EX payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the precomputed PC-relative target for branches and JAL, leaving only JALR target formation in EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX bundle so the earlier stage can carry branch/JAL destinations forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the PC-relative target alongside decod...\n  Line 7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny return stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark mixes tight loops with frequent call/return traffic. The prior\\nbackward-branch predictor did not recover enough because it ignored the\\nexpensive JALR returns that dominate many short subroutine paths.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small fetch-stage return-address stack in `if_stage.sv` and use\\nit to predict JALR returns (JALR x0, x1/x5, 0) directly in fetch. Keep\\nEX-stage redirects as the recovery path for non-return JALR and any\\nmispredicts. This should remove a high-value class of control-flow bubbles\\nwith less timing risk than a broader branch predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack, push return PCs on JAL, and speculatively steer JALR-return fetches from the stack instead of waiting for EX.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 283.5, \"delta_pct\": -8.82, \"vs_baseline\": 0.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.02, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4938989, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10613, \"ff\": 2124, \"seeds\": [140.02, 139.57, 151.91], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-16T03:47:21.033640Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.82%): A tiny fetch-side return stack only pays off if return prediction stays ...\n  Line 10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark has enough repeated loop branches that a purely reactive EX-stage\\nredirect wastes fetch bandwidth on the same hot paths over and over. The\\nprior static predictor and tiny return stack both missed too much of the real\\ncontrol-flow mix, so the next step is a predictor that learns actual branch\\nbehavior instead of assuming it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT in `rtl/if_stage.sv` with 2-bit\\nsaturating counters and stored targets for taken conditional branches and\\nJAL. Keep JALR and all mispredict recovery in EX, and update the table only\\nwhen a branch actually resolves. This should recover more loop iterations\\nthan the static backward predictor while keeping fetch-side logic narrow\\nenough to avoid another Fmax regression.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny BTB/BHT prediction table, use it to steer fetch on hot taken branches and JAL, and update it from resolved control-flow outcomes.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.34, \"delta_pct\": -0.84, \"vs_baseline\": 9.02, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.91, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4407728, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10799, \"ff\": 2518, \"seeds\":...\n  Line 15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\\nretirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\\ncombinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume t...\n  Line 18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed ID forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate copy\\nof the unforwarded source values for internal bookkeeping, while RVFI\\ncontinues to report the actual forwarded execution operands. This should\\ntrim the EX-stage critical path and lower forwarding fanout without changing\\nISA behavior or stall rules.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and older-stage writeback values into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result, while preserving the raw regfile snapshot separately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the operand muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description...\n  Line 34: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Backward-branch-only predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time in tight loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts lost ground to fetch-side bookkeeping, aliasing,\\nand Fmax pressure. A much narrower predictor that only helps the hot\\nbackward conditional-branch case should recover useful bubbles without\\ncarrying the extra state that hurt the earlier BTB, RAS, and loop variants.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends a lot of time in tight loop backedges, but the\\nbroader predictor attempts lost ground to fetch-side bookkeeping, aliasing,\\nand Fmax pressure. A much narrower predictor that only helps the hot\\nbackward conditional-branch case should recover useful bubbles without\\ncarrying the extra state that hurt the earlier BTB, RAS, and loop variants.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a branch-only fetch predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that predicts\\nbackward conditional branches as taken and steers fetch directly to the\\ncomputed branch target. Do not speculate JAL/JALR, do not add a BTB/BHT or\\nreturn stack, and keep EX-stage redirect as the recovery path for all\\nmisses. This keeps the predictor logic small while targeting the loop\\nbackedges CoreMark repeats most often.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a minimal backward-conditional-branch predictor that computes the B-type target in fetch and redirects only for predicted-taken loop backedges.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a minimal backward-conditional-branch predictor that computes the B-type target in fetch and redirects only for predicted-taken loop backedges.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 394.64, \"delta_pct\": 10.5, \"vs_baseline\": 39.54, \"fmax_mhz\": 186.22, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 471...\n  Line 37: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry backward predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow budget on a small set of\\nrepeated loop backedges. The last successful hypothesis showed that a very\\nnarrow backward-branch predictor can improve fitness without dragging in the\\nBTB, RAS, or JAL/JALR bookkeeping that hurt broader predictor attempts.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still spends most of its control-flow budget on a small set of\\nrepeated loop backedges. The last successful hypothesis showed that a very\\nnarrow backward-branch predictor can improve fitness without dragging in the\\nBTB, RAS, or JAL/JALR bookkeeping that hurt broader predictor attempts.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny two-entry tagged predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that only learns\\nbackward conditional branches. Each entry should remember the branch PC,\\ntarget, and a small taken-confidence counter so fetch can redirect early on\\nthe hottest loop backedges while cold branches still fall back to the current\\nEX-stage recovery path. Keep JAL, JALR, and forward branches reactive so the\\npredictor stays narrow and cheap to time.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny two-entry tagged predictor for backward conditional branches, with learned target/confidence state and EX redirect recovery for misses.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny two-entry tagged predictor for backward conditional branches, with learned target/confidence state and EX redirect recovery for misses.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 141.87, \"delta_pct\": -64.05, \"vs_baseline\": -49.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 67.06, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4727002, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10577, \"ff\": 2322, \"seeds\": [67.06, 62.09, 77.25], \"formal_passed\": true, \"c...\n  Line 40: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Cheaper backward predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current backward-branch predictor already proved that CoreMark benefits\\nfrom speculating loop backedges, but the fetch-side cone still pays for the\\npredictor's target math on every cycle. A narrower implementation that keeps\\nthe same prediction policy while reducing common-path logic could raise Fmax\\nwithout giving up the IPC win.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current backward-branch predictor already proved that CoreMark benefits\\nfrom speculating loop backedges, but the fetch-side cone still pays for the\\npredictor's target math on every cycle. A narrower implementation that keeps\\nthe same prediction policy while reducing common-path logic could raise Fmax\\nwithout giving up the IPC win.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the existing backward-conditional-branch prediction policy, but split\\nthe decision from target formation so fetch first classifies the instruction\\nas a backward branch and only then computes the taken target. Do not add BTB,\\nRAS, JAL/JALR speculation, or confidence state; just make the hot not-taken\\npath cheaper while preserving EX-stage redirect recovery. This should trim\\npredictor fanout in IF and retain the loop-backedge coverage that worked\\nbest so far.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the backward-branch predictor so the taken/not-taken decision is made before target formation, reducing fetch-side combinational cost while keeping the same recovery behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the backward-branch predictor so the taken/not-taken decision is made before target formation, reducing fetch-side combinational cost while keeping the same recovery behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 354.37, \"de...","metadata":{"matches":9,"truncated":false},"title":"branch compare|branch_cond|branch_target|jump_target|control-flow op|EX-stage","time":{"start":1779000097843,"end":1779000097864}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_011a8c0d65a7a301016a096321a0448193ad55b5118f23c3aa"}},"id":"prt_e34ab3c2e001NtfqybU50B7zCY","sessionID":"ses_1cb55a92dffeMp9pGqGFV