{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779000117878,"sessionID":"ses_1cb55a92dffeMp9pGqGFVEfjKE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_U3n3hhdeHBZwoPd6YdHOeoOq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r14s0\n+title: \"Gate control-flow cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The EX stage currently evaluates branch compare and target math on every\n+  instruction, even though only control-flow ops need that logic. Keeping the\n+  compare/add cone live for non-branches wastes timing budget on the common\n+  ALU path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Guard the branch-condition compare and PC-relative target math in\n+  `ex_stage.sv` so they only activate for actual branch or jump instructions.\n+  Keep JALR, misalign trapping, redirect recovery, and RVFI semantics\n+  unchanged; the only effect should be that ordinary ALU and memory ops stop\n+  paying for the always-on control-flow cone. This should trim the hot EX path\n+  enough to improve Fmax without changing architectural behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Condition branch comparison and target formation on control-flow opcodes so non-branch instructions do not carry the full control-flow cone.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r14s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt