{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779001633105,"sessionID":"ses_1cb3e19eeffeUdOgAsl15dsfjk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_2cuKf7Y5qTQNzs8AUgfGub3T","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n+  when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That keeps\n+  dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n+  stalls on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n+  the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n+  reads. Keep operand muxing, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged;\n+  only the dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear.\n+  This should recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the hot\n+  stall/forwarding path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n+  when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That keeps\n+  dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n+  stalls on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n+  the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n+  reads. Keep operand muxing, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged;\n+  only the dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear.\n+  This should recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the hot\n+  stall/forwarding path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n+title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n+  when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That keeps\n+  dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n+  stalls on payload-only encodings.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n+  the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n+  reads. Keep operand muxing, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged;\n+  only the dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear.\n+  This should recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the hot\n+  stall/forwarding path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: