ates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it keeps\\na small but hot compare cone on the PC-hold path. Moving the operand-use\\ndecision into decode should recover those stalls without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction cannot actually read one of them. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it keeps\\na small but hot compare cone on the PC-hold path. Moving the operand-use\\ndecision into decode should recover those stalls without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them only into the\\nload-use hazard check. Keep forwarding, RVFI, and the rest of the pipeline\\nunchanged; the only behavior change should be that payload-only register\\nfields no longer trigger stalls. This should improve CoreMark iter/cycle a\\nbit and slightly reduce the hazard fanout seen by Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundle so decode can carry whether rs1 and rs2 are real operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2, alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the operand-usage bits with the decoded instruction so the hazard path can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard unit while leaving the forwarding and RVFI plumbing unchang...\n  Line 24: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist immediates out of ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"After the registered IF/ID cutpoint,