le\": \"Single-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps reusing a small number of hot backward branches, but the\\nbroader predictor experiments already showed that extra BTB/RAS state can\\nerase the benefit through aliasing and fetch-side overhead. A very small\\npredictor that only remembers one hot loop backedge should be cheaper to\\nupdate and easier to time.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps reusing a small number of hot backward branches, but the\\nbroader predictor experiments already showed that extra BTB/RAS state can\\nerase the benefit through aliasing and fetch-side overhead. A very small\\npredictor that only remembers one hot loop backedge should be cheaper to\\nupdate and easier to time.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry learned predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that caches the\\ntarget and taken direction for the hottest backward conditional branch, then\\nsteers fetch early when the same PC reappears. Do not add a general BTB, RAS,\\nor JALR speculation; keep EX as the recovery path for everything else. This\\nis narrower than the prior table-based attempts and should capture the\\nrepeat-backedge behavior CoreMark actually exercises without the bookkeeping\\nthat hurt Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry learned predictor for the hottest backward conditional branch and use it to redirect fetch before EX resolves the loop backedge.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry learned predictor for the hottest backward conditional branch and use it to redirect fetch before EX resolves the loop backedge.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 220.89, \"delta_pct\": -28.96, \"vs_baseline\": -21.9, \"fmax_mhz\": 100.27, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4539290, \"iterations\"...\n  Line 26: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-usage hazard trim\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\\neven when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\\nThat leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\\ninject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\\neven when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\\nThat leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\\ninject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decode-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\\nload-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\\nKeep RVFI source snapshots and retirement behavior unchanged; only suppress\\ndead compares and false stalls on instructions whose register fields are just\\nimmediate payload. This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while\\nslightly shortening the hot hazard cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which instruction forms really read rs1 and rs2, alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream hazard logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pip...\n  Line 27: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Split slow M-extension path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\\ncombinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\\nwith the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\\ncore close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\\nCoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\\ncombinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\\nwith the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\\ncore close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\\nCoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the ALU into a fast single-cycle RV32I path and a separate slow RV32M\\nbackend for MUL/DIV/REM operations. Keep simple arithmetic, shifts, compares,\\nand branch evaluation on the fast path, then stall the pipeline only while an\\nM-operation is in flight and forward its finished result into writeback. This\\nshould remove the worst-case multiplier/divider cone from the retire-critical\\npath without changing architectural results or RVFI-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from the slow RV32M multiply/divide path, with registered completion for M-ops.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch and consume the fast-path ALU result directly, while coordinating stalls and result capture for the slow M backend.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an active M-operation as a stall condition so younger instructions wait for the slow result without corrupting retirement order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from t...\n  Line 28: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Direct-call target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is not only loop-heavy; it also revisits the same direct call sites\\nmany times. The previous branch-, return-, and loop-oriented predictors lost\\nground to aliasing, bookkeeping, or Fmax pressure because they tried to\\ncover too much control flow at once.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is not only loop-heavy; it also revisits the same direct call sites\\nmany times. The previous branch-, return-, and loop-oriented predictors lost\\nground to aliasing, bookkeeping, or Fmax pressure because they tried to\\ncover too much control flow at once.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny direct-call target cache in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that records the\\nPC and resolved target of hot JAL call sites, then steers fetch to the cached\\ntarget on a later hit. Leave conditional branches, JALR returns, and all\\nmispredict recovery in EX. Narrowing speculation to direct calls should\\nrecover repeated CoreMark subroutine-entry bubbles without the wider BTB/RAS\\nstate that hurt earlier predictor attempts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small call-target cache keyed by fetch PC, learn JAL targets from resolved redirects, and use cache hits to redirect fetch early.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small call-target cache keyed by fetch PC, learn JAL targets from resolved redirects, and use cache hits to redirect fetch early.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 276.75, \"delta_pct\": -11.0, \"vs_baseline\": -2.15, \"fmax_mhz\": 136.15, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4919525, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10945, \"ff\": 2476, \"seeds\": [144.63, 136.15, 134.05], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-17T03:55:4...","metadata":{"matches":27,"truncated":false},"title":"(structural|pipeline|fetch|branch|forward|decode|retime|stage|stall|predictor)","time":{"start":1778990273791,"end":1778990273806}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_018396a97f68d0c7016a093cc194f0819b8dfdb43a120a51b4"}},"id":"prt_e341554fc001XwDYofTF8ZOvrm","sessionID":"ses_1cbeac72cffe9EOZuzQbdpw7Cq","messageID":"msg_e3415393e001Yb8i8TZzbvOquu"}}
