{"type":"text","timestamp":1778996268918,"sessionID":"ses_1cb9051b2ffeVqmRZDcC7G7cM8","part":{"id":"prt_e3470ce67001HSSw3W8Kcp4m7j","messageID":"msg_e347064bc001h13ZKyM8W8f3tG","sessionID":"ses_1cb9051b2ffeVqmRZDcC7G7cM8","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis as a structural cut on the mispredict-recovery path: keep the predictor, but pipeline the EX-to-IF redirect so the common loop path stays fast and only rare recovery pays the extra cycle.","time":{"start":1778996268647,"end":1778996268916},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0d86b4f523b3d92e016a09542c895881948c76a24001ae175f","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778996270617,"sessionID":"ses_1cb9051b2ffeVqmRZDcC7G7cM8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_m8q2a6Ek3Jovg105PT0jRjDH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r12s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\n+title: \"Pipelined redirect recovery\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The backward-branch predictor already covers the hot loop path, so the\n+  remaining timing pressure is more likely coming from the same-cycle EX-to-IF\n+  recovery wire than from common-case fetch. Cutting that redirect path should\n+  shorten the longest control-flow cone without changing the architectural\n+  retirement model.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Register the resolved redirect from EX before IF consumes it, so mispredict\n+  recovery becomes a one-cycle recovery path instead of a same-cycle\n+  combinational override. Keep the predicted-taken fast path unchanged and\n+  preserve the exact architectural next PC in EX/RVFI; only the rare recovery\n+  case should pay the extra cycle. This should improve Fmax by removing the\n+  long EX-to-fetch feedback path that still spans branch resolution, target\n+  selection, and PC update.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Insert a registered redirect sideband between EX and IF so fetch consumes a settled recovery request instead of a live combinational one.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Produce the architecturally resolved redirect target as a latched request/target pair without changing branch, jump, or trap semantics.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Prioritize the registered recovery request over the predictor when selecting the next PC, while leaving the predicted-taken fast path intact.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/ex