{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778998317413,"sessionID":"ses_1cb71118fffesg41FnCtBKiCC8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_JBhl1CBg02nm4b9cShXZ3cW0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r13s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r13s1\n+title: \"Hoist immediates out of ID\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  ID still rebuilds immediates on every instruction even though the value is\n+  only a function of the fetched word. Moving that bit-slice out of the decode\n+  cone should shorten the common ID path without changing the pipeline contract.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a precomputed immediate field to the IF/ID bundle, generate it from the\n+  registered instruction in fetch, and have ID consume that latched value\n+  instead of instantiating `imm_gen` locally. Keep stall, flush, redirect, and\n+  RVFI behavior unchanged; this is only a structural split of the immediate\n+  construction logic so decode can spend less time on the critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the instruction immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local `imm_gen` instance.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r13s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r13s1.yaml\n=============================