cy while reducing common-path logic could raise Fmax\\nwithout giving up the IPC win.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current backward-branch predictor already proved that CoreMark benefits\\nfrom speculating loop backedges, but the fetch-side cone still pays for the\\npredictor's target math on every cycle. A narrower implementation that keeps\\nthe same prediction policy while reducing common-path logic could raise Fmax\\nwithout giving up the IPC win.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the existing backward-conditional-branch prediction policy, but split\\nthe decision from target formation so fetch first classifies the instruction\\nas a backward branch and only then computes the taken target. Do not add BTB,\\nRAS, JAL/JALR speculation, or confidence state; just make the hot not-taken\\npath cheaper while preserving EX-stage redirect recovery. This should trim\\npredictor fanout in IF and retain the loop-backedge coverage that worked\\nbest so far.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the backward-branch predictor so the taken/not-taken decision is made before target formation, reducing fetch-side combinational cost while keeping the same recovery behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the backward-branch predictor so the taken/not-taken decision is made before target formation, reducing fetch-side combinational cost while keeping the same recovery behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 354.37, \"de...","metadata":{"matches":39,"truncated":false},"title":"retime|retir|redirect|forward|hazard|branch|predict","time":{"start":1779000054692,"end":1779000054729}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0003e4a2434fdefa016a0962f688188190aacd072109e5bfd4"}},"id":"prt_e34aa93a1001r2HfNkcRrGUgfG","sessionID