tion\": \"Insert a real IF/ID register and make decode consume the registered bundle instead of the live imem output.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Insert a real IF/ID register and make decode consume the registered bundle instead of the live imem output.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 310.94, \"delta_pct\": 9.94, \"vs_baseline\": 9.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 153.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4949188, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9995, \"ff\": 1924, \"seeds\": [155.3, 144.49, 153.89], \"formal_pass...\n  Line 12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split decode from read\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ID stage still mixes decode, immediate generation, and regfile\\naccess in one cycle. After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, that combined cone\\nis the next obvious timing hotspot, so splitting it should help Fmax without\\nchanging the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction decode and immediate/control extraction into the fetch-side\\nregistered bundle, then let ID focus on operand reads and latching only the\\nalready-predecoded metadata. This should shorten the ID-stage combinational\\npath and reduce fanout from the instruction bits while keeping stall, flush,\\nredirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the predecoded bundle directly so ID only performs regfile reads and state capture.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Expand the IF/ID bundle to carry predecoded control and immediate metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predecode the registered instruction and latch the derived control bundle with the fetch output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": ...\n  Line 15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The execute stage currently pays for operand compare plus operand muxing on\\nevery instruction before it can even reach the ALU or branch compare. That\\nkeeps a wide, high-fanout forwarding cone on the retire-critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands, and let EX consume those values directly. This keeps\\nretirement and hazard behavior unchanged while shortening the execute-stage\\ncombinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume t...\n  Line 18: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed ID forwarding cut\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still resolves operand bypassing in EX, so every\\ninstruction pays for source compare and 3-way operand muxing right before\\nthe ALU or branch compare. That keeps a wide fanout cone on the retire path\\neven after fetch was already registered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate copy\\nof the unforwarded source values for internal bookkeeping, while RVFI\\ncontinues to report the actual forwarded execution operands. This should\\ntrim the EX-stage critical path and lower forwarding fanout without changing\\nISA behavior or stall rules.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and older-stage writeback values into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result, while preserving the raw regfile snapshot separately.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the operand muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add separate raw and forwarded source-operand fields to the ID/EX and MEM/WB bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description...\n  Line 21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\\nsource compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\\ncompare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\\ncycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The remaining hot cone still sits in EX, where every instruction pays for\\nsource compare plus 3-way operand muxing right before the ALU or branch\\ncompare. That bypass fanout reaches back into EX/MEM and MEM/WB on every\\ncycle, so it is a better structural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate raw\\nsource snapshot for bookkeeping, but have EX consume the already-selected\\noperands directly so the bypass cone no longer sits on the ALU and branch\\ncritical path. This should shorten the retire path and raise Fmax without\\nchanging stall, flush, or RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the operand fields so the pipeline can carry raw source reads separately from the settled execute operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and writeback data into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result while preserving the raw regfile snapshot for bookkeeping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand bypass muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the o...\n  Line 26: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-usage hazard trim\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\\neven when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\\nThat leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\\ninject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\\neven when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\\nThat leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\\ninject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decode-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\\nload-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\\nKeep RVFI source snapshots and retirement behavior unchanged; only suppress\\ndead compares and false stalls on instructions whose register fields are just\\nimmediate payload. This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while\\nslightly shortening the hot hazard cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which instruction forms really read rs1 and rs2, alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream hazard logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pip...\n  Line 30: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist immediates out of ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"ID still spends combinational time rebuilding immediates on every instruction,\\neven after fetch was turned into a registered cutpoint. That logic is\\nindependent of regfile reads and most control decisions, so moving it earlier\\nshould trim the ID-stage cone without changing the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"ID still spends combinational time rebuilding immediates on every instruction,\\neven after fetch was turned into a registered cutpoint. That logic is\\nindependent of regfile reads and most control decisions, so moving it earlier\\nshould trim the ID-stage cone without changing the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a precomputed immediate field to the IF/ID bundle, generate it in\\n`if_stage.sv` from the registered instruction, and have `id_stage.sv`\\nconsume that latched value instead of instantiating `imm_gen` locally. Keep\\nstall, flush, redirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged; this is only a pipeline\\nsplit of the immediate-construction logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the decoded immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local imm_gen instance.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the decoded immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.s...\n  Line 31: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends most of its control-flow budget in a small number of\\nhot backedges. The earlier one-entry loop predictor was too narrow,\\nwhile broader BTB/BHT and call/return schemes paid too much in fetch-\\nside bookkeeping and Fmax loss.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends most of its control-flow budget in a small number of\\nhot backedges. The earlier one-entry loop predictor was too narrow,\\nwhile broader BTB/BHT and call/return schemes paid too much in fetch-\\nside bookkeeping and Fmax loss.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny two-entry tagged loop predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that\\nlearns trip counts for backward conditional branches and predicts the\\nloop backedge until the learned exit. Keep JAL/JALR fully reactive in\\nEX and do not add a general BTB, BHT, or return stack. Two entries\\nshould cover the hottest CoreMark loops without the aliasing and\\ntiming overhead that hurt the broader predictor attempts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged two-entry loop predictor for backward conditional branches and use it to steer fetch on the hottest loop backedges.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged two-entry loop predictor for backward conditional branches and use it to steer fetch on the hottest loop backedges.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\n1 (11)\\nSBY  1:15:12 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:11 (11)\\nSBY  1:15:12 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY  1:15:12 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY  1:15:12 [insn_xor_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY  1:15:1...\n  Line 32: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Usage-gated compare cone\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\\nwhen the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That leaves\\ndead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\\nstalls on immediate, jump, fence, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\\nwhen the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That leaves\\ndead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\\nstalls on immediate, jump, fence, and SYSTEM encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\\nthe load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\\nKeep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement ordering unchanged; only the\\ndead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear. This should\\nrecover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the stall/forwarding path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pipe.\"},...\n  Line 35: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-001-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Usage-gated hazard cone\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The hot hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\\nthe younger instruction does not actually read them. That leaves dead compare\\nfanout on the stall path and can also inject false load-use bubbles on payload-\\nonly encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's control-heavy mix.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The hot hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\\nthe younger instruction does not actually read them. That leaves dead compare\\nfanout on the stall path and can also inject false load-use bubbles on payload-\\nonly encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's control-heavy mix.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\\nload-use detection and operand forwarding only fire for real source reads.\\nKeep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged; the only\\narchitectural effect should be fewer false stalls and a shorter compare cone\\non the PC-hold / bypass paths.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"fil...\n  Line 38: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-001-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Usage-gated compare cone\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The core still spends timing budget comparing raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\\nthe younger instruction does not actually read one of them. That leaves dead\\ncompare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\\nload-use stalls on payload-only encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's\\ncontrol-heavy mix.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The core still spends timing budget comparing raw rs1/rs2 fields even when\\nthe younger instruction does not actually read one of them. That leaves dead\\ncompare fanout on the hazard and forwarding paths and can also inject false\\nload-use stalls on payload-only encodings, which is wasted work on CoreMark's\\ncontrol-heavy mix.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\\nload-use detection and operand forwarding only fire for real source reads.\\nKeep operand data, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged; the only\\narchitectural effect should be fewer false stalls and a shorter compare cone\\non the PC-hold and bypass paths. This should recover a few CoreMark cycles\\nwhile also trimming the hot hazard logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2 alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"...","metadata":{"matches":11,"truncated":false},"title":"regfile|write-first|bypass","time":{"start":1779000104037,"end":1779000104081}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d05b5201facfd50016a096327eb608196986c5b0a9