ructural target than pushing more logic into fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move final rs1/rs2 forwarding selection into ID so the ID/EX register latches\\nsettled execute operands instead of raw regfile reads. Keep a separate raw\\nsource snapshot for bookkeeping, but have EX consume the already-selected\\noperands directly so the bypass cone no longer sits on the ALU and branch\\ncritical path. This should shorten the retire path and raise Fmax without\\nchanging stall, flush, or RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the operand fields so the pipeline can carry raw source reads separately from the settled execute operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route bypass selects and writeback data into ID, and feed EX from the latched forwarded operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply forwarding before latching the decode result while preserving the raw regfile snapshot for bookkeeping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand bypass muxing and consume the settled execute operands directly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the o...\n  Line 24: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist immediates out of ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, ID still pays for immediate generation\\non every instruction. That cone is independent of decode decisions and can be\\nmoved earlier without the fetch-side fanout that hurt the broader predecode\\nattempt.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"After the registered IF/ID cutpoint, ID still pays for immediate generation\\non every instruction. That cone is independent of decode decisions and can be\\nmoved earlier without the fetch-side fanout that hurt the broader predecode\\nattempt.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a precomputed immediate field to the IF/ID bundle, generate it in\\n`if_stage.sv` from the registered instruction, and let `id_stage.sv` consume\\nthat latched value directly instead of instantiating `imm_gen` again. Keep\\ndecode, stall, flush, redirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged; this only splits\\nthe immediate-slice logic out of the ID-stage cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the instruction immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local imm_gen instance.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the instruction immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local imm_gen instan...\n  Line 27: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Split slow M-extension path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\\ncombinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\\nwith the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\\ncore close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\\nCoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\\ncombinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\\nwith the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\\ncore close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\\nCoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the ALU into a fast single-cycle RV32I path and a separate slow RV32M\\nbackend for MUL/DIV/REM operations. Keep simple arithmetic, shifts, compares,\\nand branch evaluation on the fast path, then stall the pipeline only while an\\nM-operation is in flight and forward its finished result into writeback. This\\nshould remove the worst-case multiplier/divider cone from the retire-critical\\npath without changing architectural results or RVFI-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from the slow RV32M multiply/divide path, with registered completion for M-ops.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch and consume the fast-path ALU result directly, while coordinating stalls and result capture for the slow M backend.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an active M-operation as a stall condition so younger instructions wait for the slow result without corrupting retirement order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from t...\n  Line 30: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist immediates out of ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"ID still spends combinational time rebuilding immediates on every instruction,\\neven after fetch was turned into a registered cutpoint. That logic is\\nindependent of regfile reads and most control decisions, so moving it earlier\\nshould trim the ID-stage cone without changing the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"ID still spends combinational time rebuilding immediates on every instruction,\\neven after fetch was turned into a registered cutpoint. That logic is\\nindependent of regfile reads and most control decisions, so moving it earlier\\nshould trim the ID-stage cone without changing the architectural contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a precomputed immediate field to the IF/ID bundle, generate it in\\n`if_stage.sv` from the registered instruction, and have `id_stage.sv`\\nconsume that latched value instead of instantiating `imm_gen` locally. Keep\\nstall, flush, redirect, and RVFI behavior unchanged; this is only a pipeline\\nsplit of the immediate-construction logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the decoded immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local imm_gen instance.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the decoded immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.s...\n  Line 33: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Split divider from M backend\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The prior M-path split helped because the frequent RV32I path stopped sharing\\nthe multiplier/divider cone. The remaining divider work is still the widest\\narithmetic block in the core, so it is the next clean place to cut timing\\nwithout disturbing decode, forwarding, or memory behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The prior M-path split helped because the frequent RV32I path stopped sharing\\nthe multiplier/divider cone. The remaining divider work is still the widest\\narithmetic block in the core, so it is the next clean place to cut timing\\nwithout disturbing decode, forwarding, or memory behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep MUL on the fast path, but move DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a tiny iterative\\ndivider with registered state and the existing start/busy/done handshake.\\nThat removes the wide divide cone from the synthesized combinational logic\\nwhile preserving the current architectural stall model for rare M-ops. The\\ncommon RV32I/CoreMark path should close timing more easily, and the extra\\ncycles on divide/remainder should be amortized by their low frequency.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/m_backend.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the registered M backend so MUL remains fast while DIV/REM use a tiny iterative state machine instead of a wide combinational divide cone.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/m_backend.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the registered M backend so MUL remains fast while DIV/REM use a tiny iterative state machine instead of a wide combinational divide cone.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"build_failed: yosys synth: ERROR: Latch inferred for signal `\\\\m_divider.\\\\rem_shift' from always_comb process `\\\\m_divider.$proc$cores/bench/rtl/m_divider.sv:52$187'.\",...\n  Line 36: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Pipelined redirect recovery\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The backward-branch predictor already covers the hot loop path, so the\\nremaining timing pressure is more likely coming from the same-cycle EX-to-IF\\nrecovery wire than from common-case fetch. Cutting that redirect path should\\nshorten the longest control-flow cone without changing the architectural\\nretirement model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The backward-branch predictor already covers the hot loop path, so the\\nremaining timing pressure is more likely coming from the same-cycle EX-to-IF\\nrecovery wire than from common-case fetch. Cutting that redirect path should\\nshorten the longest control-flow cone without changing the architectural\\nretirement model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Register the resolved redirect from EX before IF consumes it, so mispredict\\nrecovery becomes a one-cycle recovery path instead of a same-cycle\\ncombinational override. Keep the predicted-taken fast path unchanged and\\npreserve the exact architectural next PC in EX/RVFI; only the rare recovery\\ncase should pay the extra cycle. This should improve Fmax by removing the\\nlong EX-to-fetch feedback path that still spans branch resolution, target\\nselection, and PC update.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Insert a registered redirect sideband between EX and IF so fetch consumes a settled recovery request instead of a live combinational one.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce the architecturally resolved redirect target as a latched request/target pair without changing branch, jump, or trap semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Prioritize the registered recovery request over the predictor when selecting the next PC, while leaving the predicted-taken fast path intact.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [...\n  Line 39: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Hoist immediates out of ID\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"ID still rebuilds immediates on every instruction even though the value is\\nonly a function of the fetched word. Moving that bit-slice out of the decode\\ncone should shorten the common ID path without changing the pipeline contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"ID still rebuilds immediates on every instruction even though the value is\\nonly a function of the fetched word. Moving that bit-slice out of the decode\\ncone should shorten the common ID path without changing the pipeline contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a precomputed immediate field to the IF/ID bundle, generate it from the\\nregistered instruction in fetch, and have ID consume that latched value\\ninstead of instantiating `imm_gen` locally. Keep stall, flush, redirect, and\\nRVFI behavior unchanged; this is only a structural split of the immediate\\nconstruction logic so decode can spend less time on the critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the instruction immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local `imm_gen` instance.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an immediate field to the IF/ID bundle so fetch can carry the precomputed value forward.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the instruction immediate after the fetch register and latch it with the IF/ID payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed immediate from the bundle and drop the local `imm_gen` i...\n  Line 42: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py']\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The regfile still spends combinational work on same-cycle write-first\\nbypassing for both read ports, even though the pipeline already has EX/MEM\\nand MEM/WB forwarding for real RAW hazards. Removing that read-port mux\\ncone should shorten ID without changing architected results.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the regfile's same-cycle write-first bypass and make reads return\\nonly the stored array contents, while keeping x0 hardwired to zero and the\\nexisting EX/MEM + MEM/WB forwarding network intact. That should trim the\\nhot compare/mux path on every decode cycle and let the later forwarding\\nlogic handle recency when consumers reach EX.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the write-first read-port bypass so regfile reads become plain array lookups with x0 still forced to zero.\"}]}}\n","metadata":{"matches":14,"truncated":false},"title":"structural|category: structural|\\bstructural\\b","time":{"start":1779001589097,"end":1779001589121}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04fa9007f213736b016a0968f46ec881948ea86d99399056db"}},"id":"prt_e34c1fb15001igG7BFWCBApvmy","sessionID":"ses_1cb3e1aa5ffeTByvYecnrRTjxZ","messageID":"msg_e34c1f6ef0011Tr0Dad8RSqAwA"}}
