le shortening the execute-stage\\ncombinational path and reducing fanout from EX/MEM and MEM/WB into the ALU.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume the latched operands directly in the ALU and branch logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route forwarding selects and source values into ID instead of EX, while keeping the existing hazard and RVFI plumbing intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch already-forwarded rs1/rs2 operands into the ID/EX register so downstream logic sees settled execute inputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drop the per-operand forwarding muxes and consume t...\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-aware load-use gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\\nkeeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw IF/ID register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction does not actually read rs1 or rs2. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings, and it\\nkeeps avoidable compare fanout on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny operand-usage classifier inside the hazard unit so load-use stalls\\nonly fire when the younger instruction really reads the compared source. Keep\\nforwarding, RVFI reporting, and the rest of the pipeline unchanged; only the\\nfalse dependency check should disappear. This should recover wasted CoreMark\\ncycles on payload-only register encodings with very low RTL risk.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify rs1/rs2 usage from opcode/funct fields and gate load-use compares so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction bundle into the hazard path so the interlock can classify live operands locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify rs1/rs2 usage from opcode/funct fields and gate load-use compares so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_pas...\n  Line 20: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-aware interlock trim\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use interlock still treats raw IF/ID register fields as live\\noperands, even when the younger instruction does not actually read them. That\\ncreates avoidable bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings\\nwhile keeping a hot compare cone on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use interlock still treats raw IF/ID register fields as live\\noperands, even when the younger instruction does not actually read them. That\\ncreates avoidable bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM encodings\\nwhile keeping a hot compare cone on the PC-hold path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Teach the hazard unit to classify whether the younger instruction truly reads\\nrs1 or rs2 before it checks the load-use dependency. By gating the compare on\\nreal operand usage, the core should stop stalling on payload-only register\\nfields and slightly reduce stall-path fanout, improving CoreMark iter/cycle\\nwithout changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction into the hazard path so the interlock can classify operand usage locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode rs1/rs2 usage from opcode and funct fields, then gate load-use stalls so only true operand readers can trigger them.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full IF/ID instruction into the hazard path so the interlock can classify operand usage locally.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode rs1/rs2 usage from opcode and funct fields, then gate load-use stalls so only true operand readers can trigger them.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_fai...\n  Line 23: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Decoder-gated load-use trim\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction cannot actually read one of them. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it keeps\\na small but hot compare cone on the PC-hold path. Moving the operand-use\\ndecision into decode should recover those stalls without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock still compares raw register fields even when the\\nyounger instruction cannot actually read one of them. That creates avoidable\\none-cycle bubbles on immediates, jumps, fences, and SYSTEM ops, and it keeps\\na small but hot compare cone on the PC-hold path. Moving the operand-use\\ndecision into decode should recover those stalls without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them only into the\\nload-use hazard check. Keep forwarding, RVFI, and the rest of the pipeline\\nunchanged; the only behavior change should be that payload-only register\\nfields no longer trigger stalls. This should improve CoreMark iter/cycle a\\nbit and slightly reduce the hazard fanout seen by Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundle so decode can carry whether rs1 and rs2 are real operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2, alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the operand-usage bits with the decoded instruction so the hazard path can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard unit while leaving the forwarding and RVFI plumbing unchang...\n  Line 26: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-usage hazard trim\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\\neven when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\\nThat leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\\ninject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard and forwarding logic still compares raw register fields\\neven when the younger instruction does not actually consume that operand.\\nThat leaves dead compare fanout on the PC-hold and EX bypass paths and can\\ninject avoidable bubbles on payload-only encodings.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decode-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and thread them through the pipeline so\\nload-use detection and forwarding compares only fire for real operand reads.\\nKeep RVFI source snapshots and retirement behavior unchanged; only suppress\\ndead compares and false stalls on instructions whose register fields are just\\nimmediate payload. This should recover a few wasted CoreMark cycles while\\nslightly shortening the hot hazard cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles so decode can carry whether each source is live.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which instruction forms really read rs1 and rs2, alongside the existing control outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction so downstream hazard logic can consume them without re-decoding.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decoded source-usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths while leaving RVFI operand data unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only register fields do not stall the pip...\n  Line 27: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260516-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Split slow M-extension path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\\ncombinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\\nwith the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\\ncore close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\\nCoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps RV32I ops and RV32M multiply/divide logic in one\\ncombinational block, so the common integer path still shares timing budget\\nwith the slowest M-extension cases. Isolating the slow path should let the\\ncore close timing faster on the frequent ADD/SUB/branch work that drives\\nCoreMark.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the ALU into a fast single-cycle RV32I path and a separate slow RV32M\\nbackend for MUL/DIV/REM operations. Keep simple arithmetic, shifts, compares,\\nand branch evaluation on the fast path, then stall the pipeline only while an\\nM-operation is in flight and forward its finished result into writeback. This\\nshould remove the worst-case multiplier/divider cone from the retire-critical\\npath without changing architectural results or RVFI-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from the slow RV32M multiply/divide path, with registered completion for M-ops.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch and consume the fast-path ALU result directly, while coordinating stalls and result capture for the slow M backend.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an active M-operation as a stall condition so younger instructions wait for the slow result without corrupting retirement order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the fast RV32I datapath from t...\n  Line 29: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260517-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Operand-usage gated compares\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The core still spends timing budget comparing raw r