{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779001646455,"sessionID":"ses_1cb3e1aa5ffeTByvYecnrRTjxZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_RXXTBsMvfZo3nPGVEuBdrZm3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-002-r15s1\n+title: \"Operand-liveness sideband\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use interlock still pays for raw register-field compares\n+  on instructions whose rs bits are just immediate payload. That creates\n+  avoidable bubbles and keeps avoidable logic on the stall path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny fetch-side operand-liveness sideband to the IF/ID bundle so the\n+  hazard unit can tell whether rs1 or rs2 are real inputs before it does the\n+  load-use compare. Keep full decode in ID, but stop treating payload-only\n+  register fields as live sources. This should recover false stalls on CoreMark\n+  and trim the hot hazard cone without changing ISA-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add IF/ID sideband fields for rs1/rs2 liveness so the hazard path can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute and latch the operand-liveness bits with the fetched instruction alongside the existing IF/ID bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the new IF/ID liveness sideband into the hazard unit while leaving the decode and RVFI paths unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use compares with rs1/rs2 liveness so payload-only register fields do not trigger stalls.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/core