{"type":"text","timestamp":1778991443056,"sessionID":"ses_1cbd98e14ffe0k6zPlemaqmHDm","part":{"id":"prt_e34272a41001yfRve2158HNgY3","messageID":"msg_e342712d8002PUIQVcbPR2ayOh","sessionID":"ses_1cbd98e14ffe0k6zPlemaqmHDm","type":"text","text":"I’ve settled on the narrowest predictor likely to help: static backward conditional branches only, with no JAL/JALR speculation and no learned tables. I’m writing that as the hypothesis YAML now.","time":{"start":1778991442497,"end":1778991443055},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0aea19d6815ac1dd016a0941523e248193ba435f27151b7660","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778991444920,"sessionID":"ses_1cbd98e14ffe0k6zPlemaqmHDm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_E0es531k7lZLO9lNpoHzzsqo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r11s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-003-r11s2\n+title: \"Backward-branch-only predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still spends a lot of time in tight loop backedges, but the\n+  broader predictor attempts lost ground to fetch-side bookkeeping, aliasing,\n+  and Fmax pressure. A much narrower predictor that only helps the hot\n+  backward conditional-branch case should recover useful bubbles without\n+  carrying the extra state that hurt the earlier BTB, RAS, and loop variants.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a branch-only fetch predictor in `rtl/if_stage.sv` that predicts\n+  backward conditional branches as taken and steers fetch directly to the\n+  computed branch target. Do not speculate JAL/JALR, do not add a BTB/BHT or\n+  return stack, and keep EX-stage redirect as the recovery path for all\n+  misses. This keeps the predictor logic small while targeting the loop\n+  backedges CoreMark repeats most often.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a minimal backward-conditional-branch predictor that computes the B-type target in fetch and redirects only for predicted-taken loop backedges.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r11s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r11s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experi