{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778998303996,"sessionID":"ses_1cb7111fbffeeIRUOxOfh0JI6B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_mqAfP5sIu0WWNUHZQgc4wBSO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r13s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260517-003-r13s2\n+title: \"Cheaper backward predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  The current backward-branch predictor already proved that CoreMark benefits\n+  from speculating loop backedges, but the fetch-side cone still pays for the\n+  predictor's target math on every cycle. A narrower implementation that keeps\n+  the same prediction policy while reducing common-path logic could raise Fmax\n+  without giving up the IPC win.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep the existing backward-conditional-branch prediction policy, but split\n+  the decision from target formation so fetch first classifies the instruction\n+  as a backward branch and only then computes the taken target. Do not add BTB,\n+  RAS, JAL/JALR speculation, or confidence state; just make the hot not-taken\n+  path cheaper while preserving EX-stage redirect recovery. This should trim\n+  predictor fanout in IF and retain the loop-backedge coverage that worked\n+  best so far.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Refactor the backward-branch predictor so the taken/not-taken decision is made before target formation, reducing fetch-side combinational cost while keeping the same recovery behavior.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r13s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-003-r13s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto