{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779001659156,"sessionID":"ses_1cb3e1b4affe8q0PeAfrfawTEf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4Sbz1xq4dPTKwI6NC4Thauh4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\n2: title: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n6:   when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That keeps\n7:   dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n8:   stalls on payload-only encodings.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n11:   the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n12:   reads. Keep operand muxing, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged;\n13:   only the dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear.\n14:   This should recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the hot\n15:   stall/forwarding path.\n16: expected_impact:\n17:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n18:   confidence: medium\n19: changes:\n20:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n21:     description: \"Add rs1/rs2 usage sideband bits to the pipeline bundles.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n23:     description: \"Classify which decoded instruction forms actually read rs1 and rs2.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n25:     description: \"Latch the usage bits with the decoded instruction bundle.\"\n26:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n27:     description: \"Wire the usage sideband into the hazard and forwarding paths.\"\n28:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n29:     description: \"Gate load-use compares with source-usage bits so payload-only fields do not stall the pipe.\"\n30:   - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n31:     description: \"Skip dead operand compares for instructions that do not consume a source register.\"\n\n(End of file - total 31 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260517-001-r15s0\ntitle: \"Usage-gated compare cone\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current hazard and forwarding paths still compare raw rs1/rs2 fields even\n  when the younger instruction does not actually read those operands. That keeps\n  dead compare fanout on a hot control path and can also inject false load-use\n  stalls on payload-only encodings.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add decoder-derived rs1/rs2 usage bits and carry them through the pipeline so\n  the load-use interlock and forwarding compares only fire for real operand\n  reads. Keep operand muxing, RVFI snapshots, and retirement order unchanged;\n  only the dead compare cone and payload-only false stalls should disappear.\n  This should recover a few CoreMark cycles while also shortening the hot\n  stall/forwarding path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-001-r15s0.yaml","time":{"start":1779001659150,"end":1779001659155}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_013ac8600ce4fc00016a09693b0eb48190a8781efc62a892d2"}},"id":"prt_e34c30f0d001Jf1koJl0AtdO7K","sessionID":"ses_1cb3e1b4affe8q0PeAfrfawTEf","messageID":"msg_e34c304a1001mpOMHI4LnhyVK5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779001659171,"sessionID":"ses_1cb3e1b4affe8q0PeAfrfawTEf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_DkJThUdlsi73e8mdQ48wx5S0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260517-002-r15s1\n2: title: \"Operand-liveness sideband\"\n3: category: structural\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current load-use interlock still pays for raw register-field compares\n6:   on instructions whose rs bits are just immediate payload. That creates\n7:   avoidable bubbles and keeps avoidable logic on the stall path.\n8: hypothesis: |\n9:   Add a tiny fetch-side operand-liveness sideband to the IF/ID bundle so the\n10:   hazard unit can tell whether rs1 or rs2 are real inputs before it does the\n11:   load-use compare. Keep full decode in ID, but stop treating payload-only\n12:   register fields as live sources. This should recover false stalls on CoreMark\n13:   and trim the hot hazard cone without changing ISA-visible behavior.\n14: expected_impact:\n15:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n16:   confidence: medium\n17: changes:\n18:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n19:     description: \"Add IF/ID sideband fields for rs1/rs2 liveness so the hazard path can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n20:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n21:     description: \"Compute and latch the operand-liveness bits with the fetched instruction alongside the existing IF/ID bundle.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n23:     description: \"Wire the new IF/ID liveness sideband into the hazard unit while leaving the decode and RVFI paths unchanged.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n25:     description: \"Gate load-use compares with rs1/rs2 liveness so payload-only register fields do not trigger stalls.\"\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260517-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"Operand-liveness sideband\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current load-use interlock still pays for raw register-field compares\n  on instructions whose rs bits are just immediate payload. That creates\n  avoidable bubbles and keeps avoidable logic on the stall path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny fetch-side operand-liveness sideband to the IF/ID bundle so the\n  hazard unit can tell whether rs1 or rs2 are real inputs before it does the\n  load-use compare. Keep full decode in ID, but stop treating payload-only\n  register fields as live sources. This should recover false stalls on CoreMark\n  and trim the hot hazard cone without changing ISA-visible behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add IF/ID sideband fields for rs1/rs2 liveness so the hazard path can consume them without re-decoding.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260517-002-r15s1.yaml","time":{"start":1779001659164,"end":1779001659170}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_013ac8600ce4fc00016a09693b0ec88190a1678d0b4d178a1a"}},"id":"prt_e34c30f0f001gvm2Me0bg7yGOw","sessionID":"ses_1cb3e1b4affe8q0PeAfrfawTEf","messageID":"msg_e34c304a1001mpOMHI4LnhyVK5"}}
